/* GARP SCR 学習目標（LO）別 練習問題（第8〜10章・LO 8.1〜10.10の全28LO×各3問）。自作。事実はSBTi・GHGプロトコル・PCAF・IPCC・TCFD・BCBS・IPBES・WRI等の公開一次資料で裏取り（開けなかった出典は作成報告に列挙）。GARP の教材本文・模擬試験・章末問題は使っていない */
const SCR_LO810_DATA = [
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.1] Which statement about the difference between 'net zero CO2' and 'net zero GHG' emissions is consistent with the IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report?","h":"CO2だけか全GHGか、換算指標は何かを考えます。","c":["Net zero CO2 and net zero GHG are reached at the same moment in every pathway, because the conversion metric used for non-CO2 gases does not change when the basket balances. It is the standard assumption in most published scenarios.","Net zero means that gross emissions have fallen to zero in every sector, so durably stored CO2 removals play no role in counterbalancing any remaining emissions at all.","Net zero GHG requires remaining CO2 and metric-weighted non-CO2 emissions to be counterbalanced by durably stored CO2 removals, and its timing depends on the metric (such as GWP-100) used to convert non-CO2 gases.","Net zero is reached in the year annual global emissions peak, because from that point on natural sinks are assumed to offset any further emissions from human activity. On this view the timing of balance is purely a matter of annual emission levels."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ネットゼロGHGは、残る排出(非CO2はGWP等で換算)を恒久的に貯留されるCO2除去で相殺した状態で、達成時期は換算指標に左右される。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCC AR6統合報告書のCross-Section Box 1は、ネットゼロCO2とネットゼロGHGは別物で、複数ガスの合算時期は100年GWPなどの換算指標に依存するとし、CH4・N2Oなど農業由来の一部は技術的に完全には除去できないため除去で相殺する必要があるとする。ただし、同じ排出経路なら物理的な気候応答は指標の選択に依存しない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全部門で総排出ゼロ」は定義が違う（ネットは除去を数える）。「ピーク=ネットゼロ」は排出量が減り始める時点であって均衡ではない。「同時に達成」は指標依存を無視している。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本の2050年カーボンニュートラル宣言（2020年10月）も、排出を全体としてゼロにする（排出量−吸収・除去量＝ゼロ）という同じ考え方に立つ。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.1] How does net zero relate to the Paris Agreement temperature goal, according to the IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report?","h":"気温上昇の抑制には累積CO2の上限とネットゼロCO2が必要です。","c":["Limiting warming to a specific level requires only that annual CO2 emissions stop growing, because cumulative emissions have little influence on the temperature reached.","Limiting warming to a specific level requires limiting cumulative CO2 emissions, reaching net zero or net negative CO2 emissions, and strongly reducing other GHG emissions.","Limiting warming to a specific level requires net zero in a fixed year of 2050 for every pathway, because the temperature goal itself is defined by that date.","Limiting warming to a specific level is achieved once net zero is reached, and warming then falls back automatically by the same amount within a decade."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気温上昇を一定水準に抑えるには、累積CO2排出量を制限し、ネットゼロ（またはネット負）のCO2排出に到達し、他のGHGも大幅に削減する必要がある。<br><br><b>解説</b> 統合報告書のCross-Section Box 1は、人為的な温暖化を特定の水準に抑えるには、累積CO2排出量の制限、ネットゼロまたはネット負のCO2排出、他のGHGの大幅削減が必要で、将来の追加的な温暖化は将来の排出量に依存し、総温暖化は過去・将来の累積CO2排出量に支配されるとする。パリ協定の気温目標（2℃を十分下回る、1.5℃に抑える努力）とネットゼロ目標をつなぐ関係。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「年間排出が増えなくなれば足りる」は累積の考え方に反する。「全経路で2050年固定」は気温目標が期日で定義されるという誤り。「ネットゼロで自動的に気温が戻る」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.1] A government official says: 'Global net zero cannot be reached unless every sector and every country individually reaches zero emissions.' Which response is most consistent with the IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report?","h":"部門・地域間でネガティブ排出と相殺できるかがポイントです。","c":["Global net zero can be achieved even if some sectors and regions remain net emitters, provided that others reach net negative emissions.","Global net zero can be reached only if each sector individually reaches zero gross emissions, because removals cannot be balanced against emissions from a different sector or region.","Sectors unable to reach net zero should be excluded from national targets, because a national target is credible only if it covers sectors that already have mature abatement options.","The date at which a sector reaches net zero is fixed by one scientific schedule shared by all regions, independent of cost, removal potential or available policy mechanisms."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 世界全体のネットゼロは、一部の部門・地域が排出超過でも、他がネガティブ排出になれば達成できる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 統合報告書は、部門・地域のネットゼロの有無と時期は、排出削減とCO2除去の潜在量、費用、部門・国間で排出と除去を均衡させる政策手段の有無など複数の要因で決まるとする。したがって部門ごと一律の期日はない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全部門ゼロ」「除去は部門間で相殺不可」は逆。「一律の科学的日程」は費用・潜在量・政策による違いを無視している。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.2] Which set of expectations best matches the Race to Zero 'Starting Line' criteria (Pledge, Plan, Proceed, Publish) for a member entity?","h":"4つのP：宣言・計画・実行・公表です。","c":["Pledge to reach net zero by 2060 at the latest, delay any interim target until a plan is complete, take action after validation, and report progress to members every five years.","Pledge to buy enough carbon credits to cover current emissions, set a single 2050 target without an interim step, and report progress only if a regulator requests the data.","Pledge to reduce emissions in line with national averages, adopt a plan only after the target year is reached, and publish results once at the end of the decade.","Pledge to reach net zero by 2050 at the latest with a 2030 interim target, publish a plan, take immediate action, and report progress publicly each year."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> Race to Zeroは、2050年までのネットゼロ宣言（2030年の中間目標付き）、計画の公表、即時の行動、毎年の進捗公表を求める。<br><br><b>解説</b> Race to Zero（国連気候変動枠組条約のハイレベル・チャンピオンが運営）の「Starting Line」基準は、Pledge（宣言）、Plan（計画）、Proceed（実行）、Publish（公表）の4段階で、2030年頃の中間目標と年次報告を要件とする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「2060年」「クレジットで相殺」「国の平均並み」はいずれも基準と合わない。計画を実行より後にすることや、報告を5年に1回とすることも基準に反する。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC Race to Zero, Starting Line criteria, 2022. https://climatechampions.unfccc.int/system/race-to-zero-criteria/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.2] Which set of organizations is listed by the SBTi as the partners that facilitated its growth and development?","h":"CDP、国連グローバル・コンパクトなど5者です。","c":["The UNEP Finance Initiative, the Principles for Responsible Investment, the International Energy Agency, the Institutional Investors Group on Climate Change, and the World Bank Group.","The Glasgow Financial Alliance for Net Zero, the Network for Greening the Financial System, the Basel Committee, the Financial Stability Board, and the IFRS Foundation.","CDP, the UN Global Compact, the We Mean Business Coalition, the World Resources Institute (WRI), and the World Wide Fund for Nature (WWF).","The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change, the UNFCCC Secretariat, the GHG Protocol, the Carbon Disclosure Standards Board, and the International Organization for Standardization."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SBTiの成長を支えたパートナーは、CDP・国連グローバル・コンパクト・We Mean Business連合・WRI・WWFである。<br><br><b>解説</b> SBTiは英国の慈善団体で、目標検証サービスは子会社が担う。標準・ツール・ガイダンスを整備し、企業・金融機関が科学に基づく目標を設定・検証する仕組みを提供する。ネットゼロ目標の主要プレーヤーとして、GHGプロトコル（WRI/WBCSD）やCDPと連携して使われる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> UNEP FI・PRI・IIGCCは金融系の連合で、SBTiの設立パートナーではない。GFANZ・NGFS・BCBSは金融当局・金融連合。IPCC・ISOは別の役割。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.2] A company announces 'net zero by 2040' but plans to reach it mainly by purchasing carbon credits for its current emissions, with no emissions-reduction target. Which description best identifies the central credibility problem under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard?","h":"クレジットは削減目標の達成にはカウントされません。","c":["Carbon credits do not count toward near-term or long-term science-based targets; they may only be used to neutralize residual emissions or to finance mitigation beyond targets.","Carbon credits count toward near-term targets only when retired within the same reporting year, so the plan is credible provided every credit is retired on time and fully documented.","Carbon credits may replace the long-term target only for Scope 3 emissions, so the plan is credible provided Scope 1 and 2 emissions are covered by an absolute target.","Carbon credits count toward science-based targets when they are certified by an independent registry, so the plan is credible provided each credit carries a recognised label."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> クレジットは科学に基づく削減目標の達成分に数えられず、残余排出の中和か目標を超える追加緩和の資金にだけ使える。<br><br><b>解説</b> SBTi標準は、クレジットはGHGインベントリとは別に報告し、近期・長期目標の削減分にはカウントしないとする。ネットゼロの主張には、長期目標の達成と残余排出の中和の両方が必要。ネットゼロ目標の課題は、削減のない相殺依存の目標（信頼性の欠如）にある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「年内に償却すればカウント」「Scope 3だけ代替可」「認証があればカウント」はいずれも標準に反する。認証の有無は、削減目標への算入可否を変えない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のJCM（二国間クレジット制度）やJ-クレジットも、SBTi上は削減目標に算入できず、追加の緩和や残余排出の中和という位置づけになる。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.3] Which statement correctly distinguishes Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) from long-term low greenhouse gas emission development strategies (LT-LEDS) under the Paris Agreement framework?","h":"NDCは5年サイクルの中期目標、LT-LEDSは長期戦略です。","c":["NDCs are long-term strategies fixed once for the whole century, whereas LT-LEDS are binding five-year emissions budgets that each Party must meet before the next review. It is reviewed by the Secretariat each year under its stocktake procedure.","NDCs are reviewed by the IPCC every year to set national budgets, whereas LT-LEDS are voluntary corporate plans that the UNFCCC registers for companies and cities. Credits, rather than emission cuts, are the main instrument of the strategy.","NDCs set the date for global net zero for all Parties together, whereas LT-LEDS replace NDCs once a country has reached its national peak in annual emissions.","NDCs are successive national targets communicated on a five-year cycle, whereas LT-LEDS are longer-horizon, mid-century strategies that Parties are invited to formulate and communicate."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> NDCは5年サイクルで更新する各国の削減目標、LT-LEDSは今世紀半ばを見据えた長期戦略として各国が策定・提出するよう招請されるもの。<br><br><b>解説</b> パリ協定は、各国がNDCを作成・通報・維持し（第4条2項）、5年ごとに通報する（第4条9項）としている。第4条19項は、長期の低GHG排出発展戦略の策定・通報を各国に求める（努めるべき）としている。ネットゼロ目標は、この二つの手段で国別に具体化される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「NDCが長期、LT-LEDSが拘束的5年予算」は逆。「IPCCが毎年設定」は役割が違う。「LT-LEDSがNDCを置き換える」は誤り。両者は並存する。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本は2050年カーボンニュートラルを宣言し、NDC（2030年度に2013年度比46%削減）と長期戦略（パリ協定に基づく成長戦略としての長期戦略）を国連に提出している。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, Paris Agreement, 2015. https://unfccc.int/process-and-meetings/the-paris-agreement"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.3] A government wants to reduce emissions with a price on carbon. Which statement correctly contrasts a carbon tax with an emissions trading system (ETS)?","h":"税は価格を固定し、ETSは排出量の上限を固定します。","c":["A carbon tax fixes the total quantity of emissions and lets the price vary, while an ETS fixes the price per tonne and lets the covered emissions rise or fall with the economy.","A carbon tax fixes the price per tonne and lets the quantity of emissions vary, while an ETS fixes a cap on emissions and lets the allowance price vary.","A carbon tax is paid only by households on fuel use, while an ETS covers only the power sector and cannot be extended to industrial installations or to aviation.","A carbon tax and an ETS are identical in design, because both set a cap and both let firms trade allowances, differing only in the ministry that administers them."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 炭素税は価格を決めて排出量を変動させ、ETSは排出の総量（キャップ）を決めて価格を変動させる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 炭素価格付けの二大手法。炭素税はトン当たりの税率を設定し、削減量は企業の対応で決まる。ETSは排出枠の総量を定め、取引で価格が決まる。いずれも国・地域のネットゼロ戦略の削減手段として使われる（世界銀行『State and Trends of Carbon Pricing』）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「税が量を決める」は逆。「家庭のみ」「電力のみ」は適用範囲の限定が誤り。「同一設計」は誤り。税には排出枠取引がない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本はGX推進法に基づく排出量取引制度（GX-ETS）を、2023年度からの試行を経て2026年度から本格稼働させ、直接排出量が一定規模（10万トン以上）の事業者に参加を義務づける。<br><br>【出典】World Bank, State and Trends of Carbon Pricing, annual. https://carbonpricingdashboard.worldbank.org/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.3] Which statement about the relationship between the Paris Agreement and national net-zero targets is correct?","h":"条約が各国の期日を決めるわけではありません。","c":["Article 4.1 sets a global aim of balancing emissions by sources and removals by sinks in the second half of the century, while each Party sets its own net-zero year through its NDC and long-term strategy.","Article 4.1 fixes 2050 as the legally binding net-zero year for every Party, so a national target later than 2050 would breach the treaty and trigger a compliance review. Both instruments are reviewed together at each global stocktake.","Article 4.1 requires each Party to reach net zero in the same year as the other Parties in its income group, with the group date set at each five-yearly global stocktake. Each Party sets its own national peak date inside the strategy period.","Article 4.1 sets the global aim in terms of gross emissions reaching zero by 2100, so national targets that count land-use removals are outside the agreement's scope. The two instruments are published together by the Secretariat for each Party."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> パリ協定4条1項は今世紀後半の排出と吸収の均衡を掲げるが、各国のネットゼロ時期はNDC・長期戦略で各国が決める。<br><br><b>解説</b> 第4条1項は、締約国が世界の排出ピークをできるだけ早くし、今世紀後半に人為的な排出源による排出と吸収源による除去の均衡を達成するよう急速な削減を行うとする。2050年という具体年は条約本文になく、各国が自主的に決める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「2050年に法的拘束」「所得グループ別の期日」「総排出ゼロ（2100年）」はいずれも条文にない。吸収・除去も均衡の計算に入る。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本は2020年10月に2050年カーボンニュートラルを宣言し、2021年に地球温暖化対策推進法を改正して2050年目標を基本理念に位置づけた。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, Paris Agreement, 2015. https://unfccc.int/process-and-meetings/the-paris-agreement"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.4] According to the IPCC AR6 Synthesis Report, which factors determine whether and when a given sector or region reaches net zero?","h":"削減と除去の潜在量・費用・政策手段の三つです。","c":["The sector's share of global GDP, the age of its corporate headquarters, and the number of listed companies that have already joined a voluntary net-zero campaign in the region. Each factor is weighted equally in the Synthesis Report's own cross-sector assessment.","The potential to reduce emissions and undertake carbon dioxide removal, the associated costs, and the availability of policy mechanisms to balance emissions and removals between sectors and countries.","The sector's current gross emissions alone, because a larger emitter always reaches net zero later, regardless of the cost of abatement or the availability of removal options.","The year in which the sector's national regulator first published a climate disclosure rule, because net-zero timing follows disclosure requirements rather than abatement potential. The Synthesis Report ranks these three factors by their share of sectoral emissions."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 部門・地域のネットゼロ時期は、削減・除去の潜在量、費用、部門・国間で排出と除去を均衡させる政策手段で決まる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 統合報告書のCross-Section Box 1は、ネットゼロ達成の可否と時期は、GHG削減とCO2除去の潜在量、関連費用、部門間・国間で排出と除去を均衡させる政策手段の有無など複数の要因によるとする。部門ごとに技術・資本ストック・費用が違うため、一律の時期は設定できない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「GDP比・本社の年齢・参加企業数」は無関係。「現在の総排出量だけ」は費用・除去の選択肢を無視。「開示規制の公表年」は因果が逆。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.4] Why is cement production often described as a hard-to-abate sector when planning for net zero?","h":"燃料だけでなく原料由来の排出が大きい点に注目します。","c":["Most of its direct CO2 comes from the electricity it purchases, so the sector cannot decarbonize until grid operators in its region phase out all fossil generation.","Its emissions are dominated by methane from the transport of raw materials, so the sector cannot reduce emissions without a separate methane-specific policy tool.","Its plants have very short lifetimes of about five years, so capital stock turns over too quickly to allow a coordinated decarbonization pathway for the sector.","A large share of its direct CO2 comes from the chemical calcination of limestone rather than from fuel combustion, so fuel switching alone cannot eliminate emissions."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> セメントは、石灰石の脱炭酸という化学反応による直接排出の割合が大きく、燃料転換だけではゼロにできない。<br><br><b>解説</b> セメント（クリンカー）製造では、石灰石（CaCO3）がCaOとCO2に分解する工程排出が直接CO2の過半を占める。したがってCCUS、クリンカー代替材、新セメントなどの追加策が必要で、排出削減が難しい部門とされる。設備寿命が長い（数十年）点も移行を遅らせる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「購入電力が主因」はScope 2の話で、直接排出の中心ではない。「メタンが主因」は誤り。「寿命が約5年」は逆で、実際は数十年と長い。<br><br>【出典】IEA, Tracking Cement / Technology Roadmap: Low-Carbon Transition in the Cement Industry, 2018. https://www.iea.org/energy-system/industry/cement"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.4] Under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, which long-term target year rule applies to a company using the sector-specific power sector pathway?","h":"電力・海運は他部門より早い年が求められます。","c":["The long-term target year must be 2045 or sooner, compared with 2060 or sooner for companies using the cross-sector pathway in the same standard.","The long-term target year must be 2050 or sooner, the same as for the cross-sector pathway, because the standard sets one target year for every sector.","The long-term target year must be 2040 or sooner, compared with 2050 or sooner for companies using the cross-sector pathway.","The long-term target year must be 2035 or sooner, compared with 2050 or sooner for companies using the cross-sector pathway in the same standard."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 電力（と海運）の部門別経路を使う場合、長期目標年は2040年かそれ以前で、横断経路の2050年より早い。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準は、長期目標の目標年を2050年かそれ以前とし、電力・海上輸送の部門別経路を使う目標は2040年としている。電力は再生可能エネルギーなどで他部門より早く脱炭素化でき、他部門の排出削減余地を広げる役割もある。部門の削減能力の差が目標年に反映されている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「2045/2060」「2035」は標準にない数字。「全部門で2050年」は部門別経路の規定を無視している。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.5] A company has cut its value-chain emissions by 70% from its base year by 2050 and purchases high-quality removals for the remaining 30%. Under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard, can it claim to have reached net zero?","h":"長期目標（90%以上削減）の達成が先です。","c":["Yes, because net zero only requires that emissions minus purchased removals equal zero in the target year, and the standard sets no minimum level of reduction before removals are applied to the remainder.","Yes, provided the removals are purchased from a registry-approved project, since registry approval substitutes for achieving the long-term science-based target across all scopes.","No, because a company cannot claim net zero until it has achieved its long-term science-based target across all scopes, which requires a deep reduction (at least 90% in the cross-sector pathway), and then neutralized only the residual emissions.","No, because removals can never be used under the standard; any company with residual emissions must wait until residual emissions fall to zero before claiming net zero."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 長期の科学に基づく目標（横断経路で90%以上の削減）を全スコープで達成していないので、ネットゼロは名乗れない。中和は残余分にだけ使える。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準は、ネットゼロ目標を、長期の科学に基づく削減目標と、残余排出を恒久的に中和することの両方で定義する。ほとんどの企業は長期目標で少なくとも90%削減するため、残余はおおむね10%以下。70%削減＋除去30%は、除去で深い削減を肩代わりしており要件を満たさない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「排出−除去=ゼロで足りる」は標準が否定する。「レジストリ承認で代替」も誤り。「除去は使えない」も誤りで、残余排出の中和には使う。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.5] A company that sells building insulation reports that its products avoid 2 million tCO2e a year in customers' buildings. How should this be treated under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard?","h":"回避排出は製品ライフサイクルの外側で起きる効果です。","c":["Avoided emissions can be subtracted from Scope 3 category 11 emissions in the base year, which lowers the baseline and therefore the reduction required to meet the target.","Avoided emissions occur outside the product's life cycle, so they do not count as a reduction of the company's Scope 1, 2 or 3 inventory or toward its targets.","Avoided emissions count toward the near-term target only, and must be removed from the inventory before the long-term target is assessed in the target year.","Avoided emissions count as removals under the neutralization rule, so they can be used to counterbalance residual emissions once the long-term target is met."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 回避排出は製品ライフサイクルの外で生じ、Scope 1・2・3の削減にも目標達成にも算入されない。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準は「回避排出を除外する」ことを求める。回避排出（製品がなかった場合との比較）は、製品のライフサイクル外で起こるためインベントリの削減として扱えない。WRIのガイダンスも参照。除去（炭素を大気から取り除く）とも別物。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「Scope 3から差し引く」「近期目標にだけ算入」「除去として中和に使う」はいずれも標準に反する。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.5] Which statement about 'beyond value chain mitigation' (BVCM) is correct under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard?","h":"必須ではなく推奨で、目標の達成にはカウントされません。","c":["Companies must finance BVCM equal to their residual emissions each year, and it counts as a reduction toward the near-term target when the credits are retired.","Companies can replace their long-term target with BVCM if the activity is certified by a recognised standard and is located in a developing country.","Companies must report BVCM as part of Scope 3 category 15 investments, so it is included in the inventory used to calculate the target boundary.","Companies are encouraged to invest in mitigation outside their value chains, but it is a separate element that does not replace or count toward their science-based targets."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> BVCMは自社バリューチェーン外の緩和への投資で、推奨される（should）が、科学に基づく目標の代替にも達成分にもならない。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準はネットゼロ目標の4要素（近期目標、長期目標、残余排出の中和、BVCM）の一つとしてBVCMを位置づけるが、削減目標とは別枠で、目標の達成に算入しない。社会全体のネットゼロへの貢献を促す任意の取り組み。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「毎年残余排出と同額を義務化」「長期目標の代替」「Scope 3カテゴリ15に含める」はいずれも標準にない。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.6] A company submits its near-term target to the SBTi in November 2026. Which target year is acceptable under the Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2?","h":"提出から5〜10年先（または2030年）が条件です。","c":["2033, because it falls 5 to 10 years after the date of submission.","2028, because any target year within the current five-year plan is accepted as a near-term target year.","2029, because near-term targets must fall before the 2030 date on which the global interim milestone is set.","2038, because near-term targets may be set up to twelve years ahead if the company has a long-term target."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2033年。提出から5〜10年先の目標年が近期目標として認められる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準は、近期目標の目標年を「2030年、または提出日から5〜10年先」とする。2026年11月の提出なら2031〜2036年が該当する。中間目標があることで、2050年までの経路上の道しるべになる。目標年に達したら、新しい近期目標を設定し直す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 2028・2029年は提出から5年未満。2038年は10年を超える。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.6] A company's Scope 3 emissions are 25% of its total Scope 1, 2 and 3 emissions. Under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, what is required for its Scope 3 targets?","h":"Scope 3が40%未満かどうかで近期の要件が変わります。","c":["A near-term Scope 3 target covering at least 95% of Scope 3 is required, and the long-term target may then be omitted for Scope 3.","A near-term Scope 3 target covering at least 67% of Scope 3 is required, regardless of the share of Scope 3 in total emissions.","No near-term Scope 3 target is required, but its long-term target must still cover at least 90% of mandatory Scope 3 emissions.","No Scope 3 target is required at any horizon, because Scope 3 targets are mandatory only for financial institutions."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> Scope 3が全体の40%未満なら近期のScope 3目標は不要だが、長期目標は必須Scope 3の90%以上をカバーする必要がある。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準の最小境界は、Scope 1・2は95%、Scope 3は近期で67%（Scope 3が全体の40%以上の場合）、長期は全社で90%。排出割合の小さいScope 3は近期目標の免除があるが、長期ではカバーが必須。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「95%を近期で必須」は数字がScope 1・2のもの。「割合に関係なく67%」は40%の条件を無視。「どの時点でも不要」は長期目標の要件に反する。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.6] Company A reduces emissions linearly to a 90% cut by 2050. Company B holds emissions flat until 2049, then cuts 90% in one year. Both meet the same long-term target. Why does the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard treat near-term targets as not interchangeable with long-term targets?","h":"累積排出量が気温を決めます。","c":["Near-term targets are valid only as legal evidence for regulators, so Company B's path is acceptable if the final-year level matches the long-term target.","Near-term reductions are critical to staying within the global emissions budget, and warming depends on cumulative CO2 emissions, so Company A's path emits much less in total.","Near-term and long-term targets differ only in their reporting dates, so both companies are treated as equally aligned to the carbon budget.","Near-term targets apply to Scope 3 only, so Company B's flat Scope 1 and 2 emissions are not assessed against any interim milestone."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 近期の削減は排出量予算を守るうえで重要で、気温上昇は累積排出量に依存するため、Aの経路のほうが総排出量が少ない。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準は、近期の排出削減は世界の排出予算を超えないために重要であり、長期目標とは代替できないとする。IPCCも、気温は過去・将来の累積CO2排出量で決まるとする。同じ終点でも、削減が遅いBは累積排出量が大きい。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「法的証拠」「報告日のみの違い」「近期はScope 3のみ」はいずれも標準の趣旨と異なる。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf; IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.7] A portfolio has two holdings: 60% invested in Company X with a carbon intensity of 200 tCO2e per $M revenue, and 40% in Company Y with 500 tCO2e per $M revenue. What is the portfolio's weighted average carbon intensity (WACI)?","h":"保有割合×炭素強度を足し合わせます。","c":["320 tCO2e per $M revenue (0.6 x 200 + 0.4 x 500).","380 tCO2e per $M revenue (0.4 x 200 + 0.6 x 500), where the weights were applied to the wrong holdings.","350 tCO2e per $M revenue (the simple average of the two intensities), ignoring the portfolio weights.","700 tCO2e per $M revenue (the sum of the two intensities), ignoring the portfolio weights."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> WACIは保有割合で加重した炭素強度の合計で、0.6×200＋0.4×500＝320。<br><br><b>解説</b> WACI（加重平均炭素強度）は、ポートフォリオの排出集約企業への集中度を見る指標で、単位はtCO2e/百万ドル（売上）。TCFD（2017）が資産運用者・アセットオーナー向けに提示した。PCAFもTable 2-1で、WACIをエミッション集約的な企業へのエクスポージャーを理解する指標としている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 380は加重を取り違えた値。350は単純平均、700は合計で、加重していない。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf; TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD (Annex), 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-TCFD-Annex-Amended-121517.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.7] An asset manager wants to compare the emission efficiency of power-generation companies of different sizes within the same sector. Which PCAF-listed metric is best suited?","h":"同一セクター内の効率比較には物理量あたりの排出量です。","c":["Economic emission intensity (tCO2e per $M invested), because it compares the efficiency of the companies' operations independent of the investor's position.","Absolute financed emissions (tCO2e), because they are normalized by investment size and therefore comparable across companies of different sizes.","Weighted average carbon intensity (tCO2e per $M revenue), because it measures the generation efficiency of each company per unit of electricity delivered.","Physical emission intensity (for example tCO2e per MWh generated), because it compares companies in the same sector per unit of common output."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 同じセクター内の企業を共通の産出量あたりで比べるには、物理的排出原単位（tCO2e/MWhなど）が適する。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAF（表2-1）では、物理的排出原単位は活動・産出量（MWh、製品トン等）あたりの絶対排出量で、科学に基づく目標設定や同一セクター内の比較に有用。経済的排出原単位は投融資額あたりでポートフォリオ同士の比較に使い、WACIは売上あたりで排出集約企業への集中度を見る。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 経済的原単位は投融資額あたりで、企業の運営効率ではない。絶対排出は規模に依存する。WACIは売上あたりで、発電量あたりではない。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.7] The TCFD notes a limitation of carbon footprinting and exposure metrics such as WACI when used for decision making. Which statement reflects it?","h":"排出量の指標が、そのままリスクの指標ではありません。","c":["Such metrics should not necessarily be interpreted as risk metrics; the Task Force sees reporting them as a first step toward more decision-useful, climate-related risk metrics.","Such metrics measure only physical risk exposure, so the Task Force recommends them for physical-risk analysis and discourages their use for transition-risk analysis.","Such metrics are reliable risk measures only when verified, so the Task Force recommends that they be reported only once a third-party assurance provider has verified them.","Such metrics are replaced by implied temperature rise, so the Task Force withdrew its recommendation to disclose them after the 2017 final report."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 排出量・WACIなどの指標はそのままリスク指標とは解釈できず、より意思決定に役立つ気候リスク指標への第一歩とされる。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFD実装ガイダンス（Annex）は、WACIの報告を第一歩とし、開示がより意思決定に有用な気候関連リスク指標の開発を促すと期待する。一方、現在のカーボンフットプリント指標の限界、つまりリスク指標として解釈すべきでない点も認める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「物理リスク専用」「検証済みのみ報告」「ITRに置き換えて推奨撤回」はいずれも記述にない。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Implementing the Recommendations of the TCFD (Annex), 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-TCFD-Annex-Amended-121517.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.8] A company publishes an SBTi-validated target, answers the CDP climate questionnaire and prepares IFRS S2 disclosures. Which statement best describes how these fit together in the disclosure landscape?","h":"役割が違い、算定の土台は共通です。","c":["They play the same role: each validates targets against the 1.5°C pathway, and a company needs only one of them because the others duplicate that validation. The ISSB later restored the TCFD as a separate monitoring body within the Foundation.","They play different roles: the SBTi validates targets, CDP collects questionnaire data for investors and customers, and IFRS S2 sets general-purpose reporting requirements, with each relying on GHG Protocol-based inventories.","They play different roles, but each uses its own emissions accounting method, so a company must keep three separate inventories for the three frameworks.","They play different roles, but only IFRS S2 requires an inventory, because the SBTi and CDP rely on estimates provided by data vendors for each company. IFRS S2 therefore adopts a structure based on the GHG Protocol's three scopes alone."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SBTiは目標の検証、CDPは質問票による情報収集、IFRS S2は一般目的の開示要求という別の役割で、いずれもGHGプロトコルに基づくインベントリを前提とする。<br><br><b>解説</b> ネットゼロ関連開示の主要プレーヤーの役割：SBTiは科学に基づく目標の設定・検証、CDPは投資家や購買企業の要請による質問票での情報収集、ISSBのIFRS S2は開示基準。GHGプロトコルは算定の共通の物差しで、SBTiの境界設定、IFRS S2の排出量開示とも結びつく。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全て同じ役割」は誤り。「別々の算定方法・三つのインベントリ」は不要で、共通のインベントリを使う。「IFRS S2だけがインベントリを要求」はSBTiの境界要件と矛盾する。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation (ISSB), IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, 2023. https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/; SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.8] Under IFRS S2, which statement about greenhouse gas emissions disclosure is correct?","h":"Scope 3まで含め、GHGプロトコルで測定します。","c":["An entity discloses Scope 1 and 2 only, because Scope 3 emissions remain a voluntary disclosure that the standard recommends but does not require in any circumstances.","An entity discloses net emissions after deducting carbon credits, measured in accordance with ISO 14064 only, because the standard excludes the GHG Protocol methodology.","An entity discloses gross Scope 1, 2 and 3 emissions, measured in accordance with the GHG Protocol Corporate Standard unless a jurisdictional authority requires another method.","An entity discloses emissions only for its own operations, using the equity share approach, because the standard prohibits the control approaches used in the GHG Protocol."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> IFRS S2は、Scope 1・2・3の総排出量を、GHGプロトコルの企業基準で測定して開示するよう求める（管轄区域が別の方法を求める場合を除く）。<br><br><b>解説</b> IFRS S2は、Scope 1・2・3のGHG排出量（総量）を開示し、GHGプロトコルの企業基準に従うとする。Scope 3は15カテゴリのどれを含めたかの開示も求める。クレジットの控除（ネット）は求めておらず、使用予定のクレジットは別に開示する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「Scope 3は任意」「ISO 14064のみ」「持分割合法のみ」はいずれも基準に反する。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のSSBJ基準もIFRS S2と同様に、Scope 3を含む温室効果ガス排出量の開示（算定対象としたカテゴリーの開示を含む）を求める。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation (ISSB), IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, 2023. https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch8 ネットゼロ","q":"[LO 8.8] In the net-zero disclosure landscape, which organization runs a global system in which companies answer standardized questionnaires on climate change, forests and water on behalf of investors and purchasers?","h":"質問票に回答する形で環境情報を集める非営利団体です。","c":["The ISSB, an IFRS Foundation board that operates the global questionnaires through which companies report GHG emissions to securities regulators.","The SBTi, a charity that operates the global questionnaires through which companies request validation of their near-term and long-term targets.","The GHG Protocol, a WRI and WBCSD partnership that operates the global questionnaires through which companies report verified inventories to investors.","CDP, a non-profit that operates a global environmental disclosure system based on standardized annual questionnaires."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CDPは、投資家や購買企業の要請を受け、気候変動・森林・水の標準質問票で企業の環境情報を集める非営利団体。<br><br><b>解説</b> ネットゼロ情報の開示の主要プレーヤーの役割分担：ISSBは開示基準（IFRS S1・S2）、GHGプロトコルは算定基準、SBTiは目標の設定・検証、CDPは質問票による情報収集・スコアリング。CDPはSBTiの設立パートナーでもある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ISSBは基準設定、SBTiは目標検証、GHGプロトコルは算定方法の標準化で、いずれも質問票システムの運営者ではない。<br><br>【出典】CDP, About us. https://www.cdp.net/en/info/about-us; SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.1] According to the BCBS principles on climate-related financial risks (2022), which set of steps should banks start with when building their climate risk analysis capabilities?","h":"リスクドライバーの特定、指標による数量化、伝統的リスク種別との関連づけです。","c":["Setting a fixed carbon price path for every borrower, publishing sector-wide emission caps, and obtaining the supervisor's approval of the results before any internal use.","Identifying the climate-related risk drivers that may materially impair the bank's financial condition, developing key risk indicators and metrics to quantify exposures, and assessing the links to traditional risk types such as credit and liquidity risk.","Estimating the bank's own Scope 1 and 2 emissions, buying offsets for them, and reporting the total to the market as the measure of the bank's climate-related financial risk exposure.","Waiting until the Basel Framework is amended with climate-specific capital requirements, and only then identifying which risk drivers are material to the bank's business model."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候リスク分析能力の構築は、リスクドライバーの特定、指標による露出の数量化、伝統的リスク種別との関連の評価から始める。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則（2022）のパラグラフ26は、銀行はリスク分析能力を、重要な損害を与え得るリスクドライバーの特定、露出を数量化する主要リスク指標・メトリクスの開発、気候関連金融リスクと信用・流動性などの伝統的リスク種別との関連の評価から築き始めるべきとする。原則5は、重要と評価されたリスクを自己資本・流動性の評価に反映するとする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 炭素価格の固定や監督当局の事前承認、自社排出のオフセットだけでの報告、バーゼル枠組みの改正待ちは、いずれも原則の記述にない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 金融庁は2022年7月に「金融機関における気候変動への対応についての基本的な考え方」を公表し、気候変動がもたらす機会とリスクを将来志向で認識・評価することなどを期待している。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.1] Under BCBS Principle 5, how should banks treat climate-related financial risks that have been assessed as material?","h":"重要と評価されたリスクは資本・流動性の評価に組み込みます。","c":["Banks should incorporate them into internal capital and liquidity adequacy assessment processes, including stress testing programmes where appropriate, progressively as methodologies improve.","Banks should add a fixed capital surcharge for every sector and reassess it only when the regulator publishes a new climate-risk rule for the sectors concerned.","Banks should postpone any inclusion until data and methodologies are complete for all asset classes, because partial inclusion would give a misleading picture of capital. Banks are told to apply the same adjustment to every material risk each reporting year.","Banks should limit the analysis to credit risk, because the principle excludes market, liquidity and operational risk drivers from the internal adequacy processes. Banks are told that only the supervisor may decide the timing of the inclusion."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 重要と評価した気候関連金融リスクは、必要に応じストレステストを含む内部の自己資本・流動性の十分性評価に、手法の進展に応じ漸進的に組み込む。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則5は、銀行が気候関連金融リスクを特定・数量化し、重要と評価されたものを、関連する時間軸でICAAPなどに組み込むことを求める。手法が発展途上のため、反復的・漸進的に取り込むことが想定されている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「一律の資本上乗せ」は原則にない。「データ完備まで延期」は漸進的取り込みと逆。「信用リスクのみ」は誤り。市場・流動性・オペレーショナルにも及ぶ（原則8〜11）。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.1] A small domestic bank argues that climate risk assessment does not apply to it because it has no international exposures. Which response is most consistent with the BCBS principles?","h":"規模にかかわらずリスクにさらされ、対応は比例的です。","c":["Only internationally active banks are exposed, so smaller banks may rely on the assessments of their foreign correspondent banks without their own assessment. Only banks with cross-border assets are in scope, as the principles are written for them.","All banks must apply identical methods and the same data granularity, because the principles do not allow proportionality for smaller or domestic institutions. Smaller banks apply the same expectations but are given one extra reporting year.","Banks are potentially exposed regardless of size, complexity or business model, and should manage the risks proportionately to the nature, scale and complexity of their activities.","Smaller banks are exposed only to transition risk, so they need to assess physical risk only if the supervisor issues a specific written request. Smaller banks are reviewed only by the supervisor, and not by their own board."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 銀行は規模・複雑さ・ビジネスモデルを問わずリスクにさらされ、活動の性質・規模・複雑さに比例した管理を行う。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則（2022）のパラグラフ7は、銀行は規模や複雑さ、ビジネスモデルに関係なく気候関連金融リスクにさらされる可能性があるため、個別のビジネスモデルへの影響と財務的重要性を評価し、活動の性質・規模・複雑さに比例した管理を行うべきとする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「国際行のみ」「同一手法」「移行リスクのみ」はいずれも原則に反する。比例性は認められているが、免除ではない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.2] Which statement is consistent with BCBS Principle 12 on scenario analysis?","h":"物理・移行の両方を、範囲のある時間軸で見ます。","c":["Banks should use a single central scenario to produce one loss estimate, because scenario analysis is a forecasting tool and ranges of pathways would obscure the result. This follows the standard approach of treating each risk type under its own capital buffer.","Banks should limit scenarios to transition risks over the next reporting year, because physical risks have time horizons too long for internal risk management purposes. The guide therefore applies to the bank's trading book and not to its lending business.","Banks should use scenarios only when the supervisor mandates them, because the principle describes scenario analysis as a supervisory tool rather than a bank risk tool. The guide leaves operational and liquidity risk drivers outside this treatment.","Where appropriate, banks should use scenario analysis to assess the resilience of business models and strategies to a range of plausible climate pathways, considering physical and transition risks over a range of time horizons."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 銀行は、必要に応じ、もっともらしい幅のある気候経路について、物理・移行リスクを複数の時間軸で見るシナリオ分析で、事業モデルの強靭性を評価する。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則12は、シナリオ分析で、事業モデル・戦略のレジリエンスと、リスクドライバーが信用・市場・オペレーショナル・流動性リスクに与える影響を評価するとする。脚注は、極端だがもっともらしいシナリオを検討する必要があるとする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「単一シナリオ」は幅のある経路に反する。「移行のみ・1年」は誤り。「当局が義務付けた場合のみ」も誤りで、銀行自身の管理手段でもある。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 金融庁・日本銀行は、3メガバンクと大手3損保グループとともに、NGFSのシナリオを共通シナリオとした試行的なシナリオ分析を実施している。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.2] Which statement about supervisory expectations in the BCBS climate principles is correct?","h":"監督当局の期待も比例的に設定されます。","c":["Supervisors should set one uniform set of expectations for all banks, and cross-border information sharing is prohibited by the principles to protect each jurisdiction's data. Banks are told that any exchange of supervisory information is discretionary.","Supervisors should set expectations proportionate to the nature, scale and complexity of banks' activities, and home and host supervisors of cross-border groups should share information on climate risk resilience.","Supervisors should leave climate risk entirely to bank management, and intervene only when a bank's capital ratio falls below the Basel minimum requirement. Banks are also told to wait for explicit written instructions from their home supervisor.","Supervisors should rely on banks' public disclosures alone, and should not use their own tools or follow-up measures when expectations are not met. Supervisors are expected to step in only when a bank's own metrics breach limits."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 当局は銀行の活動の性質・規模・複雑さに比例した期待を設定し、国際行グループの母国・受入国当局は情報を共有する。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則16〜18は、当局に、適切な範囲の手法とツールを使い、期待との重大な乖離に追加措置を取ること、十分な資源と能力を確保すること、シナリオ分析を使うことを求める。パラグラフ58は比例性、パラグラフ59は国際間の情報共有を述べる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「一律」「情報共有の禁止」はいずれも逆。「銀行任せ」「開示のみに依存」は、当局に適切な手法・追加措置を求める原則16と反する。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.2] The ECB's 2020 Guide on climate-related and environmental risks sets out supervisory expectations for banks. How does it expect institutions to treat these risks in their risk management?","h":"別のリスク種別ではなく、既存リスクのドライバーとして扱います。","c":["As a separate stand-alone risk type with its own capital buffer, kept outside the credit, market, operational and liquidity risk frameworks of the institution.","As a reputational matter for the communications function only, because the guide does not link climate risks to the prudential risk categories of the bank.","As drivers of existing risk categories, such as credit, market, operational and liquidity risk, rather than as a separate stand-alone risk type.","As a risk relevant only for institutions with listed equity holdings, since the guide applies its thirteen expectations to investment portfolios and not to lending."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候・環境リスクは、信用・市場・オペレーショナル・流動性リスクなど既存リスクのドライバーとして扱う。<br><br><b>解説</b> ECBガイド（2020年11月）は13の期待を示し、金融機関がこれらのリスクを既存のリスクカテゴリーに織り込むこと（独立したリスク種別ではない）、物理・移行の両面を事業環境・戦略・ガバナンス・リスク管理・開示に反映することを求める。地域のプロトコルの例。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「別個のリスク種別」「広報のみ」「上場株のみ」はいずれもガイドの趣旨に合わない。<br><br>【出典】ECB, Guide on climate-related and environmental risks, 2020. https://www.bankingsupervision.europa.eu/ecb/pub/pdf/ssm.202011finalguideonclimate-relatedandenvironmentalrisks~58213f6564.en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.3] How does IFRS S2's scenario analysis requirement differ from the TCFD recommendation?","h":"TCFDは2℃以下を推奨、S2は状況に見合う手法を求めます。","c":["The TCFD recommended using a 2°C or lower scenario, whereas IFRS S2 requires scenario analysis commensurate with the entity's circumstances and disclosure of whether a scenario aligned with the latest international agreement on climate change was used.","The TCFD required a 1.5°C scenario only, whereas IFRS S2 requires a 3°C business-as-usual scenario to be used by every entity regardless of its circumstances. Both texts treat the choice of temperature scenario as a matter for the regulator.","The TCFD did not mention scenario analysis, whereas IFRS S2 requires a quantitative model of every scenario to be audited before it can be disclosed to investors. Entities must therefore disclose results for a fixed set of three scenarios.","The TCFD and IFRS S2 are identical on scenarios, and IFRS S2 adds only a requirement to publish the scenario data as open data on the entity's website. The standards otherwise overlap fully in their scenario requirements."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TCFDは2℃以下のシナリオを推奨し、IFRS S2は状況に見合う手法を求め、最新の国際合意に整合するシナリオを使ったかの開示を求める。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFD最終報告は、2℃以下を含む複数のシナリオを推奨した。IFRS S2は、特定のシナリオを一律に指定せず、企業の状況に見合う手法でレジリエンスを評価させ、使ったシナリオ・入力・前提と、最新の国際合意に整合するか、を開示させる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「1.5℃のみ・3℃必須」「TCFDに言及なし」「同一」はいずれも事実と異なる。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation (ISSB), IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, 2023. https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/; TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (Final Report), 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.3] A small company lacks in-house climate modelling skills. How does IFRS S2 treat its approach to climate-related scenario analysis?","h":"比例性：状況に見合い、過大なコストなしで入手可能な情報です。","c":["It must buy a quantitative model from an external vendor, because IFRS S2 prohibits any qualitative approach to scenario analysis for entities of any size. Entities below a stated revenue threshold are therefore not subject to any related disclosure.","It is exempt from scenario analysis entirely, because IFRS S2 applies the requirement only to entities with more than a stated number of employees or revenues. Entities then explain the omission in a separate annual filing each year.","It must use the same scenarios as the largest listed company in its sector, because IFRS S2 requires comparability across entities within each industry. Entities of that size use the equity share method for any related reporting.","It may use an approach commensurate with its circumstances, using reasonable and supportable information available at the reporting date without undue cost or effort, which can include qualitative approaches."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 状況に見合う手法で、報告日時点で過大なコストや労力なしに入手できる合理的で裏付け可能な情報を使えばよく、定性的な手法も含まれ得る。<br><br><b>解説</b> IFRS S2は、気候レジリエンスの評価に、企業の状況に見合う気候シナリオ分析の手法を使うことを求める。報告日に過大なコストや労力なしに利用可能な合理的で裏付け可能な情報、および企業のスキル・能力・資源を考慮する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「定性的手法の禁止」「全面免除」「同業最大手と同じシナリオ」はいずれも基準にない。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation (ISSB), IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, 2023. https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.3] Which statement about the structure of IFRS S2 relative to the TCFD recommendations is correct?","h":"4本柱はTCFDから引き継がれています。","c":["IFRS S2 replaces the TCFD's four pillars with two sections, one on strategy and one on metrics, and drops governance and risk management disclosure requirements.","IFRS S2 keeps the TCFD's four pillars but removes metrics and targets, which are covered in IFRS S1 and are not repeated in the climate-specific standard.","IFRS S2 follows the structure of the GHG Protocol's scopes and has no pillar for governance, because governance is outside the ISSB's mandate.","IFRS S2 follows the TCFD's four-pillar structure of governance, strategy, risk management, and metrics and targets, and adds requirements such as industry-based metrics."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> IFRS S2はTCFDのガバナンス・戦略・リスク管理・指標と目標の4本柱を引き継ぎ、産業別指標などの要求を加えている。<br><br><b>解説</b> IFRS S2は、TCFD提言を完全に取り込み、4つの中核的内容に沿って構成する。そのうえで、産業別（SASB由来）の指標や、全業種共通の指標カテゴリーなど、TCFDより具体的な要求を加える。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「2セクション」「指標と目標の削除」「GHGプロトコル構造」はいずれも基準の構造と異なる。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation (ISSB), IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, 2023. https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.4] In the IPCC AR6 framing used for climate risk assessment, which three components combine to determine physical climate risk?","h":"ハザード・曝露・脆弱性の三つです。","c":["Probability, severity and duration, with risk arising from the product of the three for each asset.","Hazard, exposure and vulnerability, with risk arising from the interaction of the three.","Emissions, concentrations and radiative forcing, with risk arising from the sum of the three for each region.","Mitigation, adaptation and loss and damage, with risk arising from the balance of the three for each country."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 物理的な気候リスクは、ハザード・曝露・脆弱性の相互作用で決まる。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCC第6次評価報告書は、気候関連リスクを、ハザード（気候事象）、曝露（影響を受ける人や資産の存在）、脆弱性（影響の受けやすさ、適応能力）の相互作用から生じるとする（統合報告書でもリスクの次元としてハザード等を示す）。物理リスク評価の最初の整理枠組み。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「確率・深刻度・期間」「排出量・濃度・放射強制力」「緩和・適応・損失と損害」は枠組みの要素ではない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.4] According to the TCFD Technical Supplement, which sequence correctly describes the process for applying scenario analysis to climate-related risks and opportunities?","h":"最初はガバナンス、最後は文書化と開示です。","c":["Ensure governance; assess materiality; identify and define a range of scenarios; evaluate business impacts; identify potential responses; document and disclose.","Assess materiality; ensure governance; evaluate business impacts; identify a range of scenarios; document and disclose; identify potential responses.","Identify a range of scenarios; assess materiality; ensure governance; identify potential responses; evaluate business impacts; document and disclose.","Document and disclose; ensure governance; assess materiality; identify a range of scenarios; evaluate business impacts; identify potential responses."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ガバナンス確保→重要性評価→シナリオ設定→事業への影響評価→対応策の特定→文書化・開示。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFD技術補足（2017）の図2は6段階の手順を示す。1) ガバナンスの確保 2) 気候関連リスクの重要性評価 3) 幅のあるシナリオの設定 4) 事業への影響の評価（投入コスト、運営コスト、売上、サプライチェーンなど） 5) 対応策の特定 6) 文書化と開示。物理・移行リスク評価の標準的な手順。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の選択肢は、順序が入れ替わっている。重要性の評価はシナリオの前、文書化・開示は最後。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Technical Supplement: The Use of Scenario Analysis in Disclosure of Climate-Related Risks and Opportunities, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-TCFD-Technical-Supplement-062917.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.4] A coastal warehouse owner expects more frequent typhoon damage and a gradual rise in mean sea level. How does the TCFD classify these two physical risks?","h":"突発的なものが急性、長期的な変化が慢性です。","c":["Typhoon damage is a chronic physical risk, and the rise in mean sea level is an acute physical risk.","Typhoon damage is a transition risk (policy and legal), and the rise in mean sea level is a physical risk.","Typhoon damage is an acute physical risk, and the rise in mean sea level is a chronic physical risk.","Both are acute physical risks, because both affect the same warehouse in the same location over time."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 台風被害は急性の物理リスク、平均海面水位の上昇は慢性の物理リスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFD提言は、物理リスクを、急性（台風・洪水など事象に起因）と慢性（降水パターンの長期変化、平均気温の上昇、海面上昇など長期的な変化）に分ける。評価は、資産の位置データに基づく曝露とハザードの組み合わせで行う。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「台風が慢性」は逆。「移行リスク」は誤り。「どちらも急性」は慢性（長期変化）の区別を無視している。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures (Final Report), 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.5] A bank's borrower relies on a regional fishery whose collapse could disrupt an entire local economy and cascade through the loan book. Which TNFD nature-related risk category best describes the loan-book effect?","h":"生態系の不安定化が金融システムに波及するのは「システミック」です。","c":["Transition risk (policy and legal), arising from new regulation of fishing quotas that raises the borrower's compliance costs.","Systemic risk, arising from the breakdown of a whole system, with aggregated and contagion effects across the financial system.","Acute physical risk, arising from a single extreme event, such as a storm, that damages one borrower's facility in one location.","Chronic physical risk limited to one borrower, arising from gradual local warming without any effect on other borrowers."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> システミックリスク：生態系などシステム全体の崩壊が、金融システム全体に波及して生じる。<br><br><b>解説</b> TNFDは、自然関連リスクを、物理（急性・慢性）、移行（政策・法律、技術、市場、評判）、システミック（生態系の安定性の喪失、集積、伝播）に分ける。漁場の崩壊が地域経済と貸出全体へ波及する例はシステミックリスクに当たる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 規制強化は移行リスク。嵐による単一施設の被害は急性の物理リスク。局所的な温暖化は慢性の物理リスクで、他の借り手に波及しない。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Recommendations of the Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures, 2023. https://tnfd.global/recommendations-of-the-tnfd/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.5] Which statement best distinguishes nature risk from climate risk?","h":"気候は世界共通の指標、自然は場所ごとに状況が異なります。","c":["Nature risk is global and measured by one common metric, whereas climate risk is location-specific and cannot be aggregated across a company's facilities.","Nature risk concerns only the ocean realm and is measured by sea-surface temperature, whereas climate risk concerns land, freshwater and the atmosphere.","Nature risk and climate risk are identical in scope, and nature is simply the TNFD's term for the greenhouse gas inventory of the entity.","Nature risk is highly location-specific and has no single common metric, whereas a tonne of GHG has a comparable climate effect wherever it is emitted."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 自然リスクは場所固有で単一の共通指標がないが、GHGは排出場所に関係なく気候への影響が比較できる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気候変動は、CO2換算（tCO2e）という共通指標で世界の影響を集約できる。自然は、地域の生態系・流域・種ごとに状況が異なり、場所や生態系の状態に依存するため、位置情報に基づく評価が必要になる。気候変動は自然損失の要因の一つ（IPBESの五つの直接要因）でもある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「自然がグローバルで単一指標」は逆。「海洋のみ」「気候と同一」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Recommendations of the Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures, 2023. https://tnfd.global/recommendations-of-the-tnfd/; IPBES, Global Assessment Report on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services: Summary for Policymakers, 2019. https://www.ipbes.net/sites/default/files/2020-02/ipbes_global_assessment_report_summary_for_policymakers_en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.5] Which list gives the four realms of nature used by the TNFD?","h":"陸・海・淡水・大気の四つです。","c":["Land, ocean, freshwater and atmosphere, treated as the four realms of nature through which an organization locates its interface with nature.","Land, ocean, forests and soil, treated as the four realms that jointly hold all terrestrial biodiversity.","Terrestrial, marine, polar and urban, treated as the four realms by which organizations screen their sites.","Biosphere, hydrosphere, lithosphere and cryosphere, treated as the four realms of the Earth system."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TNFDの四つの領域は、陸・海・淡水・大気。<br><br><b>解説</b> TNFDは、自然を、生物多様性（生物の多様性とそれらの相互作用）を重視した自然界とし、陸域・海洋・淡水・大気の四つの領域に分ける。バリューチェーンの各拠点がどの領域と接するかを整理する枠組み。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「森林・土壌」「陸・海・極地・都市」「生物圏・水圏・岩石圏・氷圏」はTNFDの領域区分ではない。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Recommendations of the Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures, 2023. https://tnfd.global/recommendations-of-the-tnfd/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.6] According to the IPBES Global Assessment (2019), which of the five direct drivers of change in nature has had the largest global impact?","h":"土地・海の利用変化が最大です。","c":["Climate change, which IPBES ranks first among the five direct drivers, ahead of changes in land and sea use and direct exploitation of organisms.","Pollution, which IPBES ranks first among the five direct drivers, ahead of climate change and the invasion of alien species.","Changes in land and sea use, which IPBES ranks first among the five direct drivers, ahead of direct exploitation of organisms and climate change.","Invasion of alien species, which IPBES ranks first among the five direct drivers, ahead of pollution and climate change."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 最大の直接要因は、土地と海の利用変化。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPBES（2019）は、過去50年に自然に最大の世界的影響を与えた直接要因を、土地・海の利用変化、生物の直接採取、気候変動、汚染、外来種の侵入の順（影響の大きい順）とする。これらは、生産・消費パターン、人口動態などの間接要因から生じる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 気候変動は3番目。汚染は4番目。外来種は5番目。気候変動の影響は今後増すと予測されている。<br><br>【出典】IPBES, Global Assessment Report on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services: Summary for Policymakers, 2019. https://www.ipbes.net/sites/default/files/2020-02/ipbes_global_assessment_report_summary_for_policymakers_en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.6] Which of the following is NOT one of the five direct drivers of biodiversity loss identified by the IPBES Global Assessment (2019)?","h":"人口動態は直接要因ではなく間接要因です。","c":["Direct exploitation of organisms, such as overfishing and hunting, which IPBES classes among the direct drivers.","Human population dynamics, which IPBES classes among the indirect drivers underlying the direct drivers.","Pollution of air, water and soil, which IPBES classes among the direct drivers of change in nature.","Invasion of alien species, which IPBES classes among the direct drivers of change in nature."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 人口動態は間接要因で、五つの直接要因ではない。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPBESの五つの直接要因は、土地・海の利用変化、直接採取、気候変動、汚染、外来種の侵入。人口動態、生産・消費パターン、技術、ガバナンスは、直接要因を生む背景にある間接要因とされる。自然関連リスクを評価する際は、この直接要因を事業活動に結びつけて整理する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 直接採取・汚染・外来種はいずれも直接要因。<br><br>【出典】IPBES, Global Assessment Report on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services: Summary for Policymakers, 2019. https://www.ipbes.net/sites/default/files/2020-02/ipbes_global_assessment_report_summary_for_policymakers_en.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.6] In WRI's Aqueduct framework, what does the 'baseline water stress' indicator measure?","h":"取水量と利用可能な再生可能水資源の比です。","c":["The ratio of a company's water consumption to its revenue, expressed in cubic metres per million dollars of sales.","The ratio of rainfall in the driest year to the long-term average rainfall of the basin, expressed as a percentage.","The ratio of total water withdrawals to available renewable surface and groundwater supplies in a basin.","The ratio of treated wastewater discharged to total water withdrawn by industry in the basin, expressed as a percentage."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ベースラインの水ストレスは、流域の取水量の合計を、利用可能な再生可能な地表水・地下水の供給量で割った比。<br><br><b>解説</b> Aqueduct 4.0は13の水リスク指標を提供し、水ストレスは流域の取水量と利用可能な水資源の比を表す。需要の増加、供給の減少（気候変動など）が高まると水ストレスが上がる。水リスクの要因の一つ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「売上あたりの消費」は企業の原単位。「最少降雨年/平年値」「排水量/取水量」はいずれも指標の定義ではない。<br><br>【出典】WRI, Aqueduct 4.0: Updated Decision-Relevant Global Water Risk Indicators (Technical Note), 2023. https://www.wri.org/research/aqueduct-40-updated-decision-relevant-global-water-risk-indicators"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.7] Which activity belongs to the 'Evaluate' phase of the TNFD LEAP approach?","h":"依存と影響の特定は2番目のフェーズです。","c":["Identifying the environmental assets, ecosystem services, dependencies and impacts of the business at each prioritized location.","Identifying priority locations that are sensitive or material, and mapping the organization's interface with nature across its value chain.","Assessing which nature-related risks and opportunities are material, and applying existing risk management and materiality processes to them.","Setting targets, preparing the response and reporting in line with the TNFD recommended disclosures for the reporting period."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> Evaluateは、各拠点の事業の自然資産・生態系サービス・依存と影響を特定するフェーズ。<br><br><b>解説</b> LEAPはLocate（自然との接点の特定）、Evaluate（依存と影響の評価）、Assess（リスクと機会の評価）、Prepare（対応と報告の準備）の4つ。Evaluateでは、特定した拠点ごとに、どの生態系サービスに依存し、どのような影響を与えているかを整理する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 優先拠点の特定はLocate。重要なリスクと機会の評価はAssess。目標設定・報告準備はPrepare。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Guidance on the identification and assessment of nature-related issues: The LEAP approach (v1.1), 2023. https://tnfd.global/publication/additional-guidance-on-assessment-of-nature-related-issues-the-leap-approach/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.7] Which statement best describes how the TNFD recommended disclosures relate to the TCFD structure?","h":"TCFDと同じ4本柱で、14の開示事項です。","c":["The TNFD uses two pillars, nature dependencies and nature impacts, with 8 recommended disclosures, none of which is related to the TCFD structure.","The TNFD uses the same four pillars as the TCFD with 40 recommended disclosures, all of which are mandatory for organizations located in biodiversity hotspots.","The TNFD uses the LEAP phases as its four pillars, with 14 recommended disclosures that replace the TCFD's governance and risk management disclosures.","The TNFD uses the same four pillars as the TCFD (governance, strategy, risk and impact management, and metrics and targets) with 14 recommended disclosures, most adapted from the TCFD."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TNFDはTCFDと同じ4本柱で14の開示を提言し、多くはTCFDの開示事項を自然向けに応用したもの。<br><br><b>解説</b> TNFD提言（2023年9月）は、ガバナンス、戦略、リスクとインパクトの管理、指標と目標の4本柱に14の推奨開示を置く。TCFDの11項目を調整したものに、自然特有の項目が加わる。ISSBの基準との整合も図られている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「2本柱・8開示」「40開示・必須」「LEAPが4本柱」はいずれも事実と異なる。LEAPは評価の手順で、開示の柱ではない。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Recommendations of the Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures, 2023. https://tnfd.global/recommendations-of-the-tnfd/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.7] In the LEAP approach, why is the 'Locate' phase done before assessing risks?","h":"自然は場所ごとに状態が違うからです。","c":["Because the TNFD requires every organization to relocate its facilities out of sensitive ecosystems before any assessment of risks and opportunities can begin.","Because location data is needed to convert nature impacts into tCO2e, which is the single metric used throughout the TNFD framework for risk assessment.","Because nature-related dependencies, impacts and risks depend on the state of nature at specific locations, so the organization must first identify where it interfaces with nature.","Because the Locate phase sets the organization's financial targets, which the later phases then test against regulatory limits in each jurisdiction."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 自然関連の依存・影響・リスクは場所ごとの自然の状態に依存するため、先に自然との接点を特定する。<br><br><b>解説</b> LEAPのLocateは、バリューチェーンと直接操業における自然との接点を、セクター・事業活動・地理的な場所で特定する。自然リスクは場所固有のため、後続の依存・影響評価、リスク評価の前提になる。優先すべき重要・脆弱な場所も、ここで絞り込む。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「拠点の移転義務」「tCO2eへの換算」「財務目標の設定」はいずれもLocateの内容ではない。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Guidance on the identification and assessment of nature-related issues: The LEAP approach (v1.1), 2023. https://tnfd.global/publication/additional-guidance-on-assessment-of-nature-related-issues-the-leap-approach/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.8] Which description best matches the ENCORE tool used in nature risk measurement?","h":"経済活動と生態系サービスへの依存・影響を結びつけるツールです。","c":["A satellite-based tool that reports the exact tCO2e emitted at each site, to help verify the Scope 1 inventory of a company.","An online tool that maps economic activities to their dependencies and impacts on nature through ecosystem services, to help screen sectors and value chains.","A global database of the protected areas and key biodiversity areas, to help screen the proximity of a site to sensitive habitats.","A river-basin tool that scores physical quantity, quality and regulatory risks of water, to help screen sites and suppliers for water risk."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ENCOREは、経済活動と、生態系サービスを通じた自然への依存・影響を結びつけて、セクターやバリューチェーンをスクリーニングするオンラインツール。<br><br><b>解説</b> ENCORE（Exploring Natural Capital Opportunities, Risks and Exposure）は、Natural Capital Finance AllianceとUNEP-WCMCなどが開発したツールで、セクター・サブ産業・生産プロセスごとに、自然への依存と影響の程度を整理する。位置情報は含まず、拠点評価の前段階で使う。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 排出量を衛星で測るツールではない。保護区・KBAのデータはIBAT。水リスクの流域別スコアはAqueductなど。<br><br>【出典】Natural Capital Finance Alliance, ENCORE. https://encorenature.org/en"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.8] An analyst needs to screen whether a mine site is close to protected areas and key biodiversity areas. Which resource is most suitable?","h":"保護区・重要生物多様性地域のデータを提供するツールです。","c":["The Integrated Biodiversity Assessment Tool (IBAT), which provides access to data on protected areas, key biodiversity areas and the IUCN Red List.","ENCORE, which maps the dependencies of the mining sector on ecosystem services at the level of the sector without any site coordinates.","WRI Aqueduct, which scores water risk by basin but does not provide data on the protected areas or key biodiversity areas around a site.","The GHG Protocol Scope 3 Evaluator, which estimates the value-chain emissions of the mine but does not provide any biodiversity data."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 保護区・重要生物多様性地域・IUCNレッドリストのデータを提供するIBATが適する。<br><br><b>解説</b> IBAT（Integrated Biodiversity Assessment Tool）は、世界保護地域データベース、重要生物多様性地域（KBA）、IUCNレッドリストなどへのアクセスを提供し、拠点の近接性のスクリーニングに使われる。ENCOREは活動レベル、Aqueductは水リスクのツール。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ENCOREはセクターレベルで位置情報を使わない。Aqueductは水リスク。Scope 3ツールは排出量の推計で、生物多様性データを提供しない。<br><br>【出典】IBAT Alliance, IBAT. https://www.ibat-alliance.org/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.8] Which is a key challenge in measuring nature-related risk compared with measuring climate-related risk?","h":"単一の共通指標がなく、場所ごとにデータが必要です。","c":["There is one global metric for nature, but it is reported only once every ten years, so organizations cannot track change within a single reporting cycle.","Nature data are fully available and standardized across all sectors, but regulators have so far prohibited organizations from using them in risk assessments.","Nature risk can be measured only for the ocean realm, because data for the land, freshwater and atmosphere realms are not collected by any organization.","There is no single common metric like tCO2e, and the data needed (such as ecosystem condition) is local, so measurement requires location-specific data that is often incomplete."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> tCO2eのような単一の共通指標がなく、生態系の状態などのデータは地域固有で、不完全なことが多い。<br><br><b>解説</b> TNFDは、自然関連の開示が、場所固有で、動的な生態系の状態に依存し、データの入手可能性や方法論の発展途上にあることを課題として整理する。そのため、拠点データ、セクター別ツール（ENCORE）、保護区データ（IBAT）などを組み合わせて評価する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「10年に1回の単一指標」「データが完備・使用禁止」「海洋のみ」はいずれも事実と異なる。<br><br>【出典】TNFD, Recommendations of the Taskforce on Nature-related Financial Disclosures, 2023. https://tnfd.global/recommendations-of-the-tnfd/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.9] A manufacturing site withdraws 1,000 m3 of water from a river in a month and discharges 700 m3 of treated water back to the same river. What is the site's water consumption for the month?","h":"消費は、取水のうち同じ水源に戻らなかった分です。","c":["700 m3, because consumption is the water that is discharged back to the source after treatment.","1,000 m3, because consumption is the total volume withdrawn from the source, whatever is returned.","300 m3, because consumption is the water withdrawn that is not returned to the same source (for example, evaporated or incorporated into product).","1,700 m3, because consumption is the sum of the volumes withdrawn and discharged by the site."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 消費量は300 m3。取水のうち同じ水源に戻らなかった分（蒸発・製品への取り込みなど）が消費。<br><br><b>解説</b> 水リスク評価では、取水（水源から取り出す量）と消費（取水のうち同じ流域に戻らない量）を区別する。消費は、取水量−排水量（同じ水源へ）で計算する。水ストレス指標（取水量/供給量）は取水量ベース。企業の水使用量を洗い出すのが最初の作業。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 700は排水量、1,000は取水量、1,700は誤って合算している。<br><br>【出典】WRI, Aqueduct 4.0: Updated Decision-Relevant Global Water Risk Indicators (Technical Note), 2023. https://www.wri.org/research/aqueduct-40-updated-decision-relevant-global-water-risk-indicators"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.9] A basin has total water withdrawals equal to 45% of available renewable water supply. Using the Aqueduct baseline water stress categories, how is it classified?","h":"40〜80%が「高い」、80%超が「極めて高い」です。","c":["Medium-high (20-40%).","Extremely high (more than 80%).","Low-medium (10-20%).","High (40-80%)."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 45%は「高い」（40〜80%）に分類される。<br><br><b>解説</b> Aqueductの水ストレス区分は、低（10%未満）、低〜中（10〜20%）、中〜高（20〜40%）、高（40〜80%）、極めて高い（80%超）。取水量が利用可能な再生可能水資源の45%なら「高い」。拠点が流域の水ストレスの高い地域にあるかが、水リスク評価の出発点。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 20〜40%は中〜高、80%超は極めて高い、10〜20%は低〜中の区分。<br><br>【出典】WRI, Aqueduct 4.0: Updated Decision-Relevant Global Water Risk Indicators (Technical Note), 2023. https://www.wri.org/research/aqueduct-40-updated-decision-relevant-global-water-risk-indicators"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch9 気候・自然リスクの評価","q":"[LO 9.9] Which first step is most appropriate when an organization starts a water risk assessment?","h":"拠点・調達先の取水・消費と流域を把握します。","c":["Set a single company-wide water target, and apply the same percentage reduction to every facility, because water risk is the same in every basin.","Inventory its water withdrawals and consumption by facility and key supplier, and geolocate them to river basins, because water risk is basin-specific.","Buy water-stewardship credits equal to total withdrawals, because the assessment can begin only after the organization has offset its water use.","Disclose country-level average rainfall for each facility, because basin-level data are not meaningful for corporate water risk assessments."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 最初に、拠点・主要調達先ごとの取水・消費量を把握し、流域に位置づける。水リスクは流域ごとに異なる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 水リスク評価の標準的な流れは、水使用量の棚卸し、拠点・調達先の流域への位置づけ、流域の物理（量・質）・規制・評判リスクの評価、財務的重要性の判断、対応策の立案。まず、どこで、どれだけ水を使うかを把握する必要がある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全社一律の目標」は流域差を無視。「クレジットで相殺」は評価の前提ではない。「国の平均降雨」は流域単位の評価に不適切。<br><br>【出典】WRI, Aqueduct 4.0: Updated Decision-Relevant Global Water Risk Indicators (Technical Note), 2023. https://www.wri.org/research/aqueduct-40-updated-decision-relevant-global-water-risk-indicators"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.1] Which statement best distinguishes a transition plan from a net-zero target?","h":"目標は「何を・いつまでに」、計画は「どうやって」です。","c":["A target states the outcome and date, whereas a transition plan sets out the actions, resources, engagement and governance by which the organization intends to reach it.","A target is the detailed list of actions and budgets, whereas a transition plan states only the outcome and date that the organization intends to reach in the long term.","A target is prepared for investors and lenders, whereas a transition plan is prepared only for the regulator and has no use in internal strategy or capital allocation.","A target covers Scope 1 and 2 emissions, whereas a transition plan covers Scope 3 emissions and cannot refer to any of the organization's own operations."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 目標は達成する成果と期限、移行計画はそれを達成するための行動・資源・エンゲージメント・ガバナンス。<br><br><b>解説</b> TPT（移行計画タスクフォース）は、移行計画を、低GHG・気候レジリエントな経済への移行に向けた目標と行動を示す、事業戦略全体の一側面と位置づける。目標（ネットゼロの目標年など）は計画の一部で、計画は実施の中身を示す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「目標が行動リスト」は逆。「規制当局向けのみ」は用途を狭めすぎ。「Scope 1・2対3」は区別の軸が違う。<br><br>【出典】Transition Plan Taskforce, Disclosure Framework, October 2023. https://itpn.global/ (TPT materials now hosted by the IFRS Foundation / ITPN)"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.1] Which is an external use case for a company's transition plan in the financial sector?","h":"金融機関の信用判断や投資判断に使われます。","c":["Lenders and investors use client transition plans to understand clients' risk profiles and transition strategies, and to inform credit assessment and financed-emissions target setting.","Lenders use client transition plans to replace the client's financial statements in credit assessment, because a plan is regarded as sufficient evidence of repayment capacity.","Investors use client transition plans only to calculate Scope 1 emissions of the client, because plans are limited to the reporting entity's own operations.","Supervisors use client transition plans to set the capital requirements of each client company, which the client must then hold as a regulatory capital buffer."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 貸し手・投資家は、取引先の移行計画を使い、リスクの特徴と移行戦略を把握して、与信判断や投融資ポートフォリオの削減目標設定に役立てる。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則（2022）のパラグラフ32は、銀行がクライアントや取引先と積極的に関わり、追加データを集めて、移行戦略とリスクの特徴をより理解することを検討すべきとする。与信ライフサイクル全体への組み込みも求める（パラグラフ35）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「財務諸表の代替」「Scope 1のみ」「当局が資本要件を決める」はいずれも用途として誤り。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 金融庁・経済産業省・環境省は2021年5月に「クライメート・トランジション・ファイナンスに関する基本指針」を策定し（2025年版に改訂）、移行戦略を持つ企業の資金調達を後押ししている。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.1] Under IFRS S2, what is required of an entity regarding its climate-related transition plan?","h":"計画を持つことは義務ではなく、持つ場合の開示が義務です。","c":["IFRS S2 requires every entity to adopt a transition plan aligned with 1.5°C, and treats the absence of a plan as a breach of the standard for all entities.","IFRS S2 prohibits disclosure of the entity's transition plan assumptions, because such information is regarded as commercially sensitive for the investors concerned.","IFRS S2 requires a transition plan only from entities in the financial sector, and exempts non-financial entities from every disclosure about transition planning.","IFRS S2 does not require an entity to have a transition plan, but requires disclosure of information about any transition plan it has, including key assumptions and dependencies."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> IFRS S2は移行計画を持つことを求めないが、計画がある場合は主要な前提と依存関係を含む情報の開示を求める。<br><br><b>解説</b> IFRS S2のストラテジー開示は、気候関連のリスクと機会に対応するための移行計画について、主要な前提・依存関係、計画の実現方法、目標との関係などの情報を、計画がある企業に開示させる。計画を持つ義務はない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全企業に1.5℃整合の計画」「前提の開示禁止」「金融のみ」はいずれも基準にない。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation (ISSB), IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures, 2023. https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s2-climate-related-disclosures/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.2] Which set names the three principles that underpin good transition planning in the UK Transition Plan Taskforce Disclosure Framework?","h":"Ambition、Action、Accountabilityです。","c":["Assurance, Alignment and Adaptation, covering the verification of targets, the alignment of capex and the adaptation of the supply chain.","Assessment, Allocation and Audit, covering the assessment of risks, the allocation of capital and the audit of the resulting disclosures.","Ambition, Action and Accountability, covering the urgency of the entity's goals, concrete near-term steps, and robust governance and reporting.","Awareness, Approval and Announcement, covering the awareness of the board, the approval of targets and the announcement of results."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 移行計画の3原則は、Ambition（野心）、Action（行動）、Accountability（説明責任）。<br><br><b>解説</b> TPT開示フレームワーク（2023年10月）は、移行計画の策定・開示を、Ambition（目標の野心度）、Action（具体的な行動）、Accountability（ガバナンスと説明責任）の3原則に沿って整理する。戦略的で総合的な（rounded）アプローチを重視する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 3つのAで始まる語でも、他の組合せはTPTの原則ではない。<br><br>【出典】Transition Plan Taskforce, Disclosure Framework, October 2023. https://itpn.global/ (TPT materials now hosted by the IFRS Foundation / ITPN)"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.2] A company announces a 2040 net-zero target but has no capital expenditure plan, no board oversight of delivery, and no interim targets. Which principle of good transition planning is most clearly missing?","h":"目標はあるが、行動と説明責任がありません。","c":["Ambition only, because a 2040 target year is earlier than the 2050 year set for the cross-sector pathway and the company has therefore over-reached.","Action and Accountability, because the target is not supported by concrete steps, resources, oversight or milestones against which progress can be held to account.","Assurance only, because the principles require a third-party opinion on the target before the company may publish any information about it.","None, because the principles only require a target year and do not address spending, oversight, interim targets or progress reporting."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 行動（具体策・資源）と説明責任（監督・中間目標・進捗管理）が欠けている。<br><br><b>解説</b> 目標があっても、資本支出計画（Action）、取締役会の監督、中間目標・進捗管理（Accountability）がなければ、実行可能性と責任の所在が分からない。2040年の目標は野心的（Ambition）な面があり、むしろ欠けているのは実行と説明責任。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「野心過剰」は誤り。「第三者保証のみ」は原則の中身ではない。「どれも欠けていない」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】Transition Plan Taskforce, Disclosure Framework, October 2023. https://itpn.global/ (TPT materials now hosted by the IFRS Foundation / ITPN)"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.2] Which feature distinguishes a 'strategic and rounded' approach to transition planning in the TPT Disclosure Framework?","h":"自社の排出だけでなく、経済全体への移行と周辺の影響まで見ます。","c":["The plan is a standalone document prepared by the sustainability team, and is kept separate from the business strategy so that it can be updated without board approval.","The plan covers only the organization's direct operations and excludes the value chain, so that it can be completed within one reporting period.","The plan considers decarbonising the entity, responding to its own climate risks and opportunities, and contributing to an economy-wide transition, rather than focusing only on its own emissions.","The plan sets a single annual target that is revised each year in response to the carbon price, without any link to a long-term pathway."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 戦略的で総合的（strategic and rounded）な計画は、自社の脱炭素化だけでなく、自社の気候リスク・機会への対応と、経済全体の移行への貢献も含めて設計される。<br><br><b>解説</b> TPT開示フレームワーク（2023）は、戦略的野心を定め移行計画を設計する際に、自社の脱炭素化、自社の気候関連リスク・機会への対応、経済全体の移行への貢献という3つの相互に関連するチャネルを考慮し、ステークホルダー・社会・経済・自然環境への影響や依存も検討することを勧める。自社の排出目標だけに集中すると、「ペーパー脱炭素」や不適応を招き得るとする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「戦略と切り離す」「自社事業のみ」「年次目標のみ」はいずれもTPTの考え方に反する。<br><br>【出典】Transition Plan Taskforce, Disclosure Framework, October 2023. https://itpn.global/ (TPT materials now hosted by the IFRS Foundation / ITPN)"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.3] Which pair of minimum boundary coverage requirements is correct under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2?","h":"Scope 1・2は95%、長期のScope 3は90%です。","c":["Near-term targets must cover at least 67% of Scope 1 and 2 emissions, and long-term targets must cover at least 67% of mandatory Scope 3 emissions.","Near-term targets must cover at least 90% of Scope 1 and 2 emissions, and long-term targets must cover at least 95% of mandatory Scope 3 emissions.","Near-term targets must cover 100% of Scope 1 and 2 emissions, and long-term targets must cover 100% of mandatory Scope 3 emissions.","Near-term targets must cover at least 95% of Scope 1 and 2 emissions, and long-term targets must cover at least 90% of mandatory Scope 3 emissions."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 近期目標はScope 1・2の95%以上、長期目標は必須Scope 3の90%以上をカバーする。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準の表2は、Scope 1・2は95%の最小カバー、Scope 3は近期で67%（Scope 3が全体の40%以上の場合）、長期は全社で90%とする。ネットゼロ目標が実質的な削減に結びつくよう、境界の穴を小さくするための要件。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 67%は近期のScope 3の数字。90%/95%の入れ替え、100%はいずれも標準にない。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.3] Under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard, to which pathways must near-term target ambition be aligned?","h":"Scope 1・2は1.5℃、Scope 3はwell-below 2℃です。","c":["Scope 1 and 2 targets must be aligned with 1.5°C pathways, and Scope 3 targets must be aligned with at least well-below 2°C pathways.","Scope 1 and 2 targets must be aligned with well-below 2°C pathways, and Scope 3 targets must be aligned with 1.5°C pathways.","Scope 1, 2 and 3 targets must all be aligned with 3°C pathways, since the standard sets one minimum temperature level for every scope.","Scope 1 and 2 targets must be aligned with 1.5°C pathways, and Scope 3 targets are exempt from any temperature alignment requirement."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 近期目標は、Scope 1・2が1.5℃経路、Scope 3がwell-below 2℃以上の経路に整合させる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準の脚注は、2022年7月以降、Scope 1・2の近期目標に1.5℃整合、Scope 3の近期目標にwell-below 2℃整合を求めているとする。ネットゼロ標準では、長期の目標は1.5℃整合の経路に沿う。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「入れ替え」は逆。「3℃」はパリ協定の目標水準より高い。「Scope 3は免除」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.3] An oil and gas company sells fuels to customers. Under the SBTi Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, how must use-phase emissions from sold or distributed fossil fuels be treated in its targets?","h":"販売した化石燃料の使用段階は、別の排出削減目標が必要です。","c":["They may be excluded from the target boundary if they are below 5% of total Scope 3 emissions, because the standard sets a de minimis threshold for this source.","They must be covered by a separate emission reduction target, irrespective of how small their share of total emissions is.","They must be covered by an intensity target only, because absolute targets are not permitted for sold or distributed fossil fuels under the standard.","They may be neutralized with carbon credits in place of reduction, because the standard treats sold fuels as residual emissions from the start."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 販売・流通した化石燃料の使用段階排出は、別の排出削減目標（シェアに関わらず）でカバーする必要がある。<br><br><b>解説</b> 標準の基準C4・C37は、販売・流通した化石燃料の使用段階排出は別の排出削減目標（シェアに関わらず）でカバーするとする。化石燃料関連の事業者の、移行の責任の大きな部分を目標に含めるための規定。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「5%未満は除外」「原単位のみ」「クレジットで中和」はいずれも標準の記述にない。クレジットは削減目標に算入されない。<br><br>【出典】SBTi, Corporate Net-Zero Standard v1.3.2, 2026. https://sciencebasedtargets.org/resources/files/Net-Zero-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.4] Which list gives the five elements of a good practice transition plan in the TPT Disclosure Framework?","h":"基盤・実施戦略・エンゲージメント戦略・指標と目標・ガバナンスです。","c":["Foundations, risk assessment, scenario analysis, metrics and targets, and assurance.","Ambition, action, accountability, engagement strategy, and implementation strategy.","Foundations, implementation strategy, engagement strategy, metrics and targets, and governance.","Governance, strategy, risk management, metrics and targets, and financial planning."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 5要素は、Foundations（基盤）、Implementation strategy（実施戦略）、Engagement strategy（エンゲージメント戦略）、Metrics and targets（指標と目標）、Governance（ガバナンス）。<br><br><b>解説</b> TPT開示フレームワークは、移行計画の開示を5つの要素に整理する。基盤は戦略的な野心と前提、実施戦略は事業運営・製品・方針・財務計画、エンゲージメント戦略はバリューチェーン・業界・政府などへの働きかけ、指標と目標はGHG排出量・目標・クレジット、ガバナンスは取締役会の監督・経営陣の責任・組織文化など。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「リスク評価・シナリオ分析」は別の整理。「Ambition・Action・Accountability」は原則で、要素ではない。「戦略・リスク管理…」はTCFD/ISSBの4本柱に近い。<br><br>【出典】Transition Plan Taskforce, Disclosure Framework, October 2023. https://itpn.global/ (TPT materials now hosted by the IFRS Foundation / ITPN)"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.4] A bank's transition plan describes a programme to engage its high-emitting clients, lobby for supportive public policy, and collaborate with industry bodies. Which TPT element does this belong to?","h":"バリューチェーン・業界・政府への働きかけです。","c":["Engagement strategy.","Implementation strategy.","Foundations.","Metrics and targets."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> エンゲージメント戦略に属する。<br><br><b>解説</b> TPTのエンゲージメント戦略は、バリューチェーン（顧客・サプライヤー）、業界、政府・公共部門、コミュニティ・市民社会への働きかけを扱う。金融機関では、高排出クライアントへのエンゲージメントや、政策提言がここに含まれる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 実施戦略は自社の事業運営・製品・方針・財務計画。基盤は野心と前提。指標と目標は数値の枠組み。<br><br>【出典】Transition Plan Taskforce, Disclosure Framework, October 2023. https://itpn.global/ (TPT materials now hosted by the IFRS Foundation / ITPN)"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.4] A company's transition plan says that executive pay is linked to emissions targets, the board's sustainability committee oversees delivery, and staff receive training on the plan. Which TPT element does this belong to?","h":"取締役会の監督・報酬・スキルは別の要素です。","c":["Engagement strategy.","Governance.","Implementation strategy.","Metrics and targets."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ガバナンスに属する。<br><br><b>解説</b> TPTのガバナンス要素は、取締役会の監督、経営陣の役割と責任、組織文化、スキルとインセンティブ（報酬との連動）、従業員への訓練などを扱う。計画の実行を担保する仕組み。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> エンゲージメントは外部への働きかけ。実施戦略は事業運営・財務計画。指標と目標は数値指標の開示。<br><br>【出典】Transition Plan Taskforce, Disclosure Framework, October 2023. https://itpn.global/ (TPT materials now hosted by the IFRS Foundation / ITPN)"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.5] Company A owns 40% of a joint venture and does not operate it; its partner holds the remaining 60% and has full authority over operating policies. The venture emits 50,000 tCO2e. How much does Company A report under (i) the equity share approach and (ii) the operational control approach?","h":"持分は40%、運営権限は相手方にあります。","c":["(i) 50,000 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 20,000 tCO2e under operational control.","(i) 0 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 50,000 tCO2e under operational control.","(i) 30,000 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 50,000 tCO2e under operational control.","(i) 20,000 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 0 tCO2e under operational control."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 持分割合法では20,000 tCO2e、オペレーショナルコントロール法では0。<br><br><b>解説</b> 持分割合法は経済的持分（ここでは40%）に応じた排出量（50,000×40%＝20,000）を計上する。オペレーショナルコントロール法は、自社またはその子会社が運営方針を導入・実行する完全な権限を持つ事業の排出量の100%を計上し、そうでなければ計上しない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 50,000は全体、30,000は相手方の持分。20,000を支配法に使うのも誤り。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Accounting and Reporting Standard (Revised Edition), 2004, Chapter 3. https://ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/standards/ghg-protocol-revised.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.5] Company B holds 30% of a facility but operates it with full authority to introduce and implement operating policies. The facility emits 10,000 tCO2e. How much does Company B report under (i) equity share and (ii) operational control?","h":"運営権限があれば、持分に関係なく100%です。","c":["(i) 10,000 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 3,000 tCO2e under operational control.","(i) 3,000 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 10,000 tCO2e under operational control.","(i) 7,000 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 3,000 tCO2e under operational control.","(i) 3,000 tCO2e under equity share, and (ii) 0 tCO2e under operational control."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 持分割合法では3,000 tCO2e、オペレーショナルコントロール法では10,000 tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> 運営者である企業は、オペレーショナルコントロール法で、持分に関係なく排出量の100%を計上する。持分割合法では、30%の持分に応じ3,000 tCO2e。統合方法の選択で、同じ事業の排出量が変わる例。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 入れ替えは誤り。7,000は他の出資者の持分。支配法で0は、運営者であることと矛盾する。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Accounting and Reporting Standard (Revised Edition), 2004, Chapter 3. https://ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/standards/ghg-protocol-revised.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.5] Which statement about the financial control approach in the GHG Protocol Corporate Standard is correct?","h":"経済的利益を得るために財務・運営方針を指示する能力です。","c":["A company has financial control only if it owns more than 50% of the voting shares, regardless of the economic substance of its relationship with the operation.","A company has financial control if it has full authority to introduce operating policies, so the criterion is identical to operational control in every case.","A company has financial control if it holds any equity interest, and the standard then requires 100% of the operation's emissions to be reported.","A company has financial control if it can direct the financial and operating policies of the operation to gain economic benefits, and may have it even with less than a 50% interest."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 財務支配とは、経済的利益を得るために運営の財務・運営方針を指示できる能力で、持分が50%未満でも成立し得る。<br><br><b>解説</b> GHGプロトコル企業基準は、財務支配では法的形式より経済的実質が優先され、子会社として連結される事業であれば支配を持つとする。関連会社（重要な影響力のみ）は財務支配ではなく、支配法では0%。統合の方針は組織全体に一貫して適用する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「50%超の議決権のみ」は実質優先の原則に反する。「運営権限が全て同一」は誤り。「持分があれば100%」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Accounting and Reporting Standard (Revised Edition), 2004, Chapter 3. https://ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/standards/ghg-protocol-revised.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.6] A company's facility uses 4,000 MWh of purchased electricity (location-based emission factor 0.45 tCO2e/MWh) and its fleet burns 50,000 litres of petrol (emission factor 2.30 kgCO2e/litre). What are its total Scope 1 and 2 emissions?","h":"単位をtCO2eにそろえて足します。","c":["1,915 tCO2e (1,800 from electricity plus 115 from petrol).","1,800 tCO2e, counting only the purchased electricity and leaving out the fleet petrol emissions.","116,800 tCO2e, adding the petrol emissions in kgCO2e to the electricity emissions in tCO2e.","6,400 tCO2e, adding the electricity use in MWh to the petrol emissions after a unit conversion."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 電力1,800＋ガソリン115＝1,915 tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> 活動量×排出係数で計算する。購入電力（Scope 2）は4,000×0.45＝1,800 tCO2e。ガソリン（Scope 1）は50,000 L×2.30 kg/L＝115,000 kg＝115 tCO2e。合計1,915 tCO2e。単位（kg→t）の換算が重要。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 1,800はScope 1の脱落。116,800は単位の混在。6,400は活動量の単位（MWh）の足し算で意味がない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本の温対法に基づく算定・報告・公表（SHK）制度でも、活動量×排出係数（電気は電気事業者ごとの排出係数）で算定する。<br><br>【出典】WRI/WBCSD, GHG Protocol Corporate Accounting and Reporting Standard (Revised Edition), 2004, Chapter 3. https://ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/standards/ghg-protocol-revised.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.6] A site emits 5 tonnes of methane (CH4, GWP-100 = 28) and 0.4 tonnes of nitrous oxide (N2O, GWP-100 = 265) in a year. What are the site's emissions in tCO2e?","h":"各ガスに地球温暖化係数（GWP）を掛けて合計します。","c":["5.4 tCO2e, adding the tonnes of the two gases without applying the global warming potentials.","1,336.2 tCO2e, applying the N2O GWP to the methane and the CH4 GWP to the nitrous oxide.","246 tCO2e (5 x 28 = 140, plus 0.4 x 265 = 106).","2,460 tCO2e, applying the correct GWPs but misplacing the decimal point in the final sum."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 5×28＋0.4×265＝140＋106＝246 tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> CO2換算量（tCO2e）は、各ガスの排出量にGWPを掛けて合計する。ここでの係数は、IPCC第5次評価報告書の100年GWP（CH4 28、N2O 265）。GHGプロトコルは最新のAR6の値の使用を推奨している。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 5.4はGWPの適用漏れ。1,336.2は係数の取り違え。2,460は桁の誤り。<br><br>【出典】GHG Protocol, Global Warming Potential Values (v2.0, August 2024). https://ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/2024-08/Global-Warming-Potential-Values%20%28August%202024%29.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.6] Using the GHG Protocol's recommended AR6 GWP-100 values (fossil methane 29.8, nitrous oxide 273), what are the emissions of 2 tonnes of fossil methane and 3 tonnes of nitrous oxide in tCO2e?","h":"AR6の係数：化石由来メタン29.8、N2O 273です。","c":["878.6 tCO2e (2 x 29.8 = 59.6, plus 3 x 273 = 819).","855.0 tCO2e, applying the AR5 values (30 for fossil methane and 265 for nitrous oxide).","635.4 tCO2e, applying the GWP of nitrous oxide to the methane and that of methane to the nitrous oxide.","5.0 tCO2e, adding the tonnes of the two gases without applying any global warming potential."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2×29.8＋3×273＝59.6＋819＝878.6 tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> GHGプロトコルは、2024年8月の更新で、最新のAR6のGWP値の使用を推奨している。化石燃料の漏出に由来するメタンには「化石由来」の29.8、その他の発生源は非化石由来の27.0を使う。N2Oは273。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 855.0はAR5の値。635.4は係数の取り違え。5.0はGWPの適用漏れ。<br><br>【出典】GHG Protocol, Global Warming Potential Values (v2.0, August 2024). https://ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/2024-08/Global-Warming-Potential-Values%20%28August%202024%29.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.7] A financial institution wants to compare the emissions intensity of two portfolios of different sizes per dollar invested. Which PCAF metric is the most suitable?","h":"投融資額あたりの排出量で、規模の違うポートフォリオを比べます。","c":["Absolute emissions (tCO2e), because they are already normalized to the size of each portfolio.","Physical emission intensity (tCO2e per MWh), because it is expressed per dollar of the investee's revenue.","Economic emission intensity (tCO2e per $M loaned or invested), because it normalizes the emissions attributed to each portfolio by the amount financed.","Data quality score (1 to 5), because it measures the emissions per dollar for each asset class."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 投融資額あたりの経済的排出原単位（tCO2e/百万ドル）が適する。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFの表2-1は、絶対排出量は気候への影響と基準値、経済的排出原単位は異なるポートフォリオ同士の比較、物理的排出原単位は共通の産出量あたりの効率、WACIは排出集約企業への集中度を見る指標とする。金融機関は、まず絶対排出量を開示する（PCAFは絶対排出量の開示を求める）。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 絶対排出量は規模に依存。物理的原単位は産出量あたりで、ドルあたりではない。データ品質スコアは排出量ではなくデータの質。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.7] Which statement about PCAF's reporting requirements for financed emissions is correct?","h":"絶対排出量を開示し、除去と回避は別に報告します。","c":["Financial institutions shall disclose only emission intensities, and may net emission removals and avoided emissions against financed emissions in the reported total.","Financial institutions shall disclose absolute financed emissions, and shall report emission removals and avoided emissions separately from their Scope 1, 2 and 3 inventories.","Financial institutions shall disclose absolute financed emissions only for Scope 1 and 2 of investees, and may leave Scope 3 of investees out of the report at any time.","Financial institutions shall disclose financed emissions only if verified at reasonable assurance, because unverified estimates may not be reported at all."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 絶対排出量の開示が必須で、除去・回避排出は、金融機関のScope 1・2・3とは別に報告する。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFは、金融機関が絶対的なファイナンスド・エミッションを開示すること、除去と回避排出の報告はScope 1・2・3インベントリとは別に行うことを求める。投融資先のScope 3は、段階的導入（2025年以降は全セクター）。検証は、時間をかけて限定的保証以上を目指す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「原単位のみ」「ネッティング可」は誤り。「Scope 3は常に除外可」は段階導入の要件と矛盾。「合理的保証のみ報告可」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.7] Which exposure is NOT one of the seven asset classes covered by the PCAF Global GHG Standard Part A (Second Edition, 2022)?","h":"ローン・投資の7つの資産クラスです。","c":["Project finance.","Motor vehicle loans.","Sovereign debt.","Unsecured credit-card receivables."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 無担保のクレジットカード債権は、Part Aの7つの資産クラスに含まれない。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFのPart A（第2版）の7資産クラスは、上場株式・社債、事業向け融資・非上場株式、プロジェクトファイナンス、商業用不動産、住宅ローン、自動車ローン、ソブリン債。ソブリン債は第2版で追加された。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> プロジェクトファイナンス、自動車ローン、ソブリン債はすべて対象。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.8] A bank holds $20M of bonds issued by a listed company with an enterprise value including cash (EVIC) of $400M and annual emissions of 150,000 tCO2e. What are the bank's financed emissions?","h":"分母は上場企業ではEVICです。","c":["7,500 tCO2e (attribution factor = 20/400 = 5%).","3,750 tCO2e, where the EVIC was taken as $800M.","30,000 tCO2e, where the attribution factor was taken as 20% instead of 5%.","750 tCO2e, where the decimal point was misplaced in the attribution factor."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 帰属係数20/400＝5%、7,500 tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFでは、上場株式・社債の帰属係数は、未払残高÷EVIC（時価総額＋負債の簿価＋少数株主持分、現金は控除しない）。ファイナンスド・エミッション＝帰属係数×投融資先の排出量＝5%×150,000＝7,500。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 3,750はEVICの誤り。30,000は帰属係数の誤り。750は桁の誤り。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.8] A bank has an outstanding mortgage of $240,000 on a home valued at $400,000 at origination. The home's annual emissions are 8 tCO2e. What are the bank's financed emissions for this mortgage?","h":"住宅ローンの分母は、組成時の物件価値です。","c":["3.2 tCO2e, where the attribution factor was taken as 40%, the share of the homeowner's equity.","8.0 tCO2e, where the bank was assigned all of the emissions of the home.","4.8 tCO2e (attribution factor = 240,000 / 400,000 = 60%).","1.9 tCO2e, where the attribution factor was taken as 24%."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 帰属係数は240,000/400,000＝60%、4.8 tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFの住宅ローン・商業用不動産では、帰属係数は、未払残高÷組成時の物件価値（土地・建物・改良を含む）。建物の年間排出量×帰属係数＝8×60%＝4.8。分母は組成時の価値に固定される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 3.2は自己資金分の40%。8.0は全量の帰属。1.9は係数の誤り。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.8] A bank lends $30M to a project whose total equity plus debt is $200M. The project emits 80,000 tCO2e a year. What are the bank's financed emissions for the project?","h":"プロジェクトでは、分母はそのプロジェクトの自己資本＋負債です。","c":["2,400 tCO2e, where the attribution factor was taken as 3%.","24,000 tCO2e, where the attribution factor was taken as 30%.","80,000 tCO2e, where the bank was assigned all emissions of the project.","12,000 tCO2e (attribution factor = 30/200 = 15%)."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 帰属係数は30/200＝15%、12,000 tCO2e。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFのプロジェクトファイナンスでは、帰属係数は、金融機関の投融資残高÷プロジェクトの自己資本と負債の合計。80,000×15%＝12,000。株式・債務の双方で、プロジェクトの排出量が全額帰属するようにする設計で、二重計上を避ける。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 2,400と24,000は係数の誤り。80,000は全量の帰属。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.9] For listed equity and corporate bonds in the PCAF data quality hierarchy, which data supports the best data quality score (score 1)?","h":"検証された、企業報告の排出量です。","c":["Emissions estimated from the company's revenue and sector average emission factors per unit of revenue (Option 3a).","Verified emissions reported by the company, with the outstanding amount and EVIC known (Option 1a).","Emissions calculated from the company's production data and emission factors specific to that primary data (Option 2b).","Emissions estimated from sector asset turnover ratios and emission factors per unit of revenue (Option 3c)."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 最高のスコア1は、検証済みの企業報告排出量（オプション1a）。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFのデータ品質スコアは、1（最高品質）から5（最低品質）。上場株式・社債では、スコア1が検証済みの企業排出量、物理的活動量に基づく推計（スコア2〜3）、経済的活動に基づく推計（スコア4〜5）の順に、確実性が下がる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 売上ベースの推計はスコア4、生産データに基づく計算はスコア3、資産回転率・売上あたり係数による推計は最低のスコア5。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.9] A bank's business loans: Loan A $600M with data quality score 2, Loan B $300M with score 4, and Loan C $100M with score 5. What is the exposure-weighted data quality score?","h":"未払残高で加重平均します。","c":["3.7, the simple average of the three scores, which ignores the outstanding amounts.","4.0, the median of the three scores, which ignores the outstanding amounts.","3.5, the average of the best and the worst data quality scores of the portfolio.","2.9, calculated as (600 x 2 + 300 x 4 + 100 x 5) / 1,000."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 加重平均スコアは(600×2＋300×4＋100×5)÷1,000＝2.9。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFは、資産クラス・セクターごとに、未払残高で加重したデータ品質スコアを開示すること（またはできない場合は説明すること）を求める。式：Σ(未払残高×スコア)÷Σ未払残高。Scope 3の加重スコアは、Scope 1・2とは別に報告する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 3.7は単純平均。4.0は中央値。3.5は最良と最悪の平均で、加重していない。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.9] A bank has a mortgage for which it knows the floor area and the official building energy label, but no metered energy data. Under the PCAF mortgage data quality table, which score applies?","h":"エネルギーラベルと床面積から推計する場合です。","c":["Score 1 (Option 1a: metered actual energy consumption with supplier-specific emission factors).","Score 5 (Option 3: estimated consumption per building from building type and location statistics, with the number of buildings).","Score 3 (Option 2a: estimated consumption per floor area from official energy labels, with the floor area known).","Score 2 (Option 1b: metered actual energy consumption with average emission factors specific to the energy source)."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> スコア3（オプション2a：公的な省エネラベルに基づく床面積あたりの推計と床面積）。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFの住宅ローンでは、スコア1は実測のエネルギー消費量と供給者別の排出係数、スコア2は実測と平均係数、スコア3は公的ラベルと床面積に基づく推計、スコア4は建物タイプ・地域の統計と床面積、スコア5は建物タイプ・地域統計と建物数に基づく推計。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> スコア1・2は実測データが必要。スコア5は建物数のみ。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.10] Beyond mandatory disclosure rules, which driver pushes corporate borrowers to adopt transition plans, according to the BCBS climate principles?","h":"銀行は与信の全期間で、取引先の移行戦略を確認します。","c":["Banks are prohibited from lending to any client without a validated science-based target, so every borrower must have one before onboarding. Banks are expected to confirm each client's target with the supervisor before any onboarding.","Banks are expected to incorporate climate-related risks into the entire credit life cycle, including client due diligence and ongoing monitoring, and to engage clients to understand their transition strategies.","Banks are expected to rely on the credit rating agencies' climate scores alone, so clients need only maintain a rating to satisfy their lenders.","Banks are expected to set the interest rate of every loan from the client's published emissions, so clients adopt plans solely for pricing reasons. Banks are expected to pass each client's data to an external provider for approval."],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 銀行は、与信の全期間（顧客デューデリジェンス・継続モニタリング）に気候リスクを組み込み、顧客の移行戦略を理解するために働きかける。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則のパラグラフ35は、気候関連リスクを、顧客のオンボーディングの顧客デューデリジェンスや継続的なモニタリングを含む与信ライフサイクル全体に組み込むことを求める。パラグラフ32は、取引先に積極的に働きかけ、追加データを集めて移行戦略を理解することを検討すべきとする。開示義務以外の、金融機関からの需要という採用の動機。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「SBT無しは融資禁止」「格付け会社のスコアのみ」「排出量で金利を一律設定」はいずれも原則にない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.10] Which PCAF requirement creates demand from financial institutions for corporate clients to produce emissions data and plans?","h":"投融資先のScope 3は2025年以降、全セクターで求められます。","c":["PCAF's phase-in for including investees' Scope 3 emissions: by reports published in 2025 onwards, every sector is required.","PCAF's requirement that every client of a financial institution obtain a data quality score of 1 by 2025 or be excluded from the portfolio.","PCAF's requirement that clients publish a transition plan certified by PCAF before the financial institution may report financed emissions.","PCAF's requirement that clients buy carbon credits equal to their financed emissions, which the financial institution then retires on their behalf."],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 投融資先のScope 3の算入について、2025年以降の報告からすべてのセクターが対象となる段階導入。<br><br><b>解説</b> PCAFは、EUのTEGの段階導入に沿い、投融資先のScope 3の算入を、2021年以降はエネルギー（石油・ガス）と鉱業、2023年以降は運輸・建設・建物・素材・産業、2025年以降はすべてのセクターに広げることを求める。金融機関は、取引先から、より詳細なデータを求めるようになる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全員スコア1」「PCAFの認証」「クレジット購入の義務」はいずれもPCAFの要件ではない。<br><br>【出典】PCAF, The Global GHG Accounting and Reporting Standard Part A: Financed Emissions, Second Edition, 2022. https://carbonaccountingfinancials.com/files/downloads/PCAF-Global-GHG-Standard.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch10 移行計画と炭素報告","q":"[LO 10.10] A bank finds that its clients' emissions data are unavailable or not comparable. Which action does the BCBS climate principles suggest?","h":"取引先への働きかけと、暫定的な代理指標です。","c":["Wait until all clients publish verified data before reporting any climate-related financial risk exposures, because proxies are not allowed in internal reports.","Exclude clients without data from the climate analysis altogether, because the principles apply only to clients that report emissions data under a mandatory rule.","Assign the sector's highest emission figure to every client without data, because the principles require the most conservative assumption in all cases.","Consider actively engaging clients and counterparties to collect additional data, and, where reliable data are unavailable, use reasonable proxies and assumptions as an intermediate step."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 取引先に働きかけて追加データを集めることを検討し、信頼できるデータがない場合は、暫定的に合理的な代理指標と仮定を使う。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS原則のパラグラフ32は、移行戦略とリスクの特徴をより理解するため、取引先に積極的に働きかけ、追加データを集めること、信頼できる比較可能なデータがない場合には、内部報告で合理的な代理指標と仮定を、中間的な手段として使えるとする。取引先にとっては、移行計画やデータを整備する動機になる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全データが揃うまで待つ」「データなしの顧客を除外」「最高値を一律適用」はいずれも原則にない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Principles for the effective management and supervision of climate-related financial risks, 2022. https://www.bis.org/publications/202206-guidelines-principles-effective-management-and-supervision-climate-related-financial-risks.pdf"}
];
